1
00:00:01,170 --> 00:00:03,830
Et tu sais, j'ai encore les marques de tes dents sur mon poignet.
And you know, I still have your teeth marks on my wrist.

2
00:00:04,640 --> 00:00:05,540
Pas sûr que ça parte.
Not sure that's going away.

3
00:00:05,780 --> 00:00:07,040
Je suis désolée, mon chou.
I'm sorry, sweetheart.

4
00:00:07,880 --> 00:00:10,780
Non, moi, j'ai juste un être humain qui a traversé mes entrailles.
No, me, I just had a human being tear through my insides.

5
00:00:10,940 --> 00:00:12,640
Excuse-moi.
Excuse me.

6
00:00:12,740 --> 00:00:13,460
Sans anesthésie.
Without anesthesia.

7
00:00:13,720 --> 00:00:14,720
Non, mais c'est moi, je suis bête.
No, it's me, I'm being silly.

8
00:00:16,140 --> 00:00:18,220
Mais c'était fou, Andrea. Fou.
But it was insane, Andrea. Insane.

9
00:00:19,650 --> 00:00:21,890
Déjà que t'étais mon héroïne, alors là, alors là, c'est...
You were already my hero, but now, now it's just...

10
00:00:21,890 --> 00:00:23,610
Ouais, je crois qu'on s'en souviendra un peu.
Yeah, I think we'll remember this one for a while.

11
00:00:24,210 --> 00:00:24,850
Ah ben...
Well...

12
00:00:26,720 --> 00:00:27,980
Comment elle s'appelle, alors ?
So what's her name?

13
00:00:27,980 --> 00:00:28,580
Flora.
Flora.

14
00:00:29,060 --> 00:00:31,390
Bon, Flora.
Right, Flora.

15
00:00:33,110 --> 00:00:35,910
Et tu sais, moi aussi, j'ai trouvé un nom pour notre bébé.
And you know, I also found a name for our baby.

16
00:00:36,900 --> 00:00:40,780
C'est l'agent fait le bonheur qui t'en dit.
It's "Happiness Agent" — what do you think?

17
00:00:42,530 --> 00:00:44,710
Allô ? Andrea, t'es là ?
Hello? Andrea, you there?

18
00:00:44,710 --> 00:00:47,550
Euh, ouais, ouais, ouais. Je sais pas.
Uh, yeah, yeah, yeah. I don't know.

19
00:00:47,570 --> 00:00:49,630
C'est bien, non, l'agent fait le bonheur ?
It's good, right? Happiness Agent?

20
00:00:51,120 --> 00:00:52,000
C'est le bonheur !
It's happiness itself!

21
00:00:52,980 --> 00:00:55,580
Le bonheur, quand ça se passe comme ça, avec des gens raisonnables,
Happiness — when it goes like this, with reasonable people,

22
00:00:56,020 --> 00:00:58,640
des gens qui savent de quoi ils parlent, qui respectent le travail des autres,
people who know what they're talking about, who respect each other's work,

23
00:00:58,740 --> 00:00:59,100
mais évidemment.
but of course.

24
00:01:00,900 --> 00:01:01,460
Bon, super.
Great, perfect.

25
00:01:01,980 --> 00:01:02,980
Ben, on se rappelle.
Well, we'll talk soon.

26
00:01:03,320 --> 00:01:04,380
Hein ? Salut.
Hm? Bye.

27
00:01:05,910 --> 00:01:06,630
Ça va ?
You okay?

28
00:01:06,630 --> 00:01:08,950
Ouais, y a un truc que je comprends pas bien dans tes contrats, alors.
Yeah, there's something I don't quite get in your contracts.

29
00:01:09,770 --> 00:01:11,290
Isabelle Huppert, en ce moment, elle tourne bien dans...
Isabelle Huppert — right now, she's shooting in...

30
00:01:11,290 --> 00:01:12,730
She's a femme fatale, de Gary Sedwick ?
She's a Femme Fatale, by Gary Sedwick?

31
00:01:12,730 --> 00:01:14,150
Ouais. Ça vient de commencer.
Yeah. That just started.

32
00:01:14,890 --> 00:01:17,050
Et elle tourne aussi dans Marie-Médicis, de Cédric Kahn.
And she's also shooting Marie de Médicis, by Cédric Kahn.

33
00:01:17,290 --> 00:01:19,410
Oui. C'est presque fini, ça, d'ailleurs.
Yes. That one's almost wrapped, actually.

34
00:01:19,570 --> 00:01:21,670
D'accord. Sauf que là, dans le contrat américain,
Right. Except here, in the American contract,

35
00:01:22,070 --> 00:01:23,170
il y a écrit exclusive.
it says exclusive.

36
00:01:24,420 --> 00:01:26,140
Ça veut dire contrat d'exclusivité.
That means an exclusivity clause.

37
00:01:26,160 --> 00:01:26,580
Et c'est net.
And it's clear-cut.

38
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:30,060
Donc, normalement, elle a pas le droit de tourner dans un autre film en même temps.
So technically, she's not allowed to shoot another film at the same time.

39
00:01:30,160 --> 00:01:30,620
C'est bien ça ?
Is that right?

40
00:01:31,780 --> 00:01:33,340
C'est juste pour que je comprenne.
Just so I understand.

41
00:01:33,460 --> 00:01:35,460
Non. Alors, je t'explique, c'est juste un léger chevauchement.
No. Let me explain — it's just a slight overlap.

42
00:01:35,500 --> 00:01:36,020
Ça n'a rien à voir.
It's completely different.

43
00:01:36,320 --> 00:01:38,440
Un léger chevauchement dont tout le monde est parfaitement au courant ?
A slight overlap that everyone is perfectly aware of?

44
00:01:38,440 --> 00:01:39,380
Non, pas vraiment, mais...
No, not exactly, but...

45
00:01:39,740 --> 00:01:41,120
Donc, qu'est-ce que t'as foutu, Gabriel ?
So what the hell did you do, Gabriel?

46
00:01:41,120 --> 00:01:42,500
Là, on est complètement hors-la-loi.
We're completely operating outside the law here.

47
00:01:42,660 --> 00:01:45,580
Mais rien, quoi. J'ai fait mon boulot d'agent, Hicham.
Nothing, really. I was doing my job as an agent, Hicham.

48
00:01:46,680 --> 00:01:47,800
Isabelle Huppert, c'est une icône.
Isabelle Huppert is an icon.

49
00:01:47,880 --> 00:01:49,760
C'est une espèce de légende vivante, comme ça.
She's something of a living legend, you know.

50
00:01:49,980 --> 00:01:50,740
Tout le monde la veut.
Everyone wants her.

51
00:01:50,920 --> 00:01:52,240
Et elle, quand il y a un beau rôle qui passe,
And when a great role comes along,

52
00:01:52,420 --> 00:01:54,820
elle est passionnée, alors elle veut pas le louper.
she's passionate — she doesn't want to miss it.

53
00:01:54,940 --> 00:01:57,640
Du coup, on s'arrange. D'accord ? On se débrouille.
So we make it work. Okay? We figure it out.

54
00:01:57,960 --> 00:02:00,720
Parce que sinon, on représente pas Isabelle Huppert, tu comprends ?
Because otherwise, we don't represent Isabelle Huppert, you understand?

55
00:02:00,720 --> 00:02:02,340
Et Isabelle Huppert, elle ira voir un autre agent.
And Isabelle Huppert will go find another agent.

56
00:02:02,700 --> 00:02:04,440
Voilà. Donc, si on l'aime, on fait avec.
There it is. So if you love her, you deal with it.

57
00:02:05,370 --> 00:02:05,990
Moi, je l'aime.
I love her.

58
00:02:06,370 --> 00:02:08,170
Ouais, mais comment elle fait concrètement ?
Yeah, but how does she actually manage it?

59
00:02:08,170 --> 00:02:08,970
Non, mais c'est très simple.
No, it's very simple.

60
00:02:09,570 --> 00:02:11,410
Le jour, elle tourne pour les Américains,
Days, she shoots for the Americans,

61
00:02:11,430 --> 00:02:14,030
et la nuit, pour les Français.
and at night, for the French.

62
00:02:14,170 --> 00:02:16,770
Mais ça dure que trois jours, et il en reste plus que deux.
But it only lasts three days, and there are only two left.

63
00:02:17,580 --> 00:02:18,320
Mais c'est impossible.
But that's impossible.

64
00:02:19,020 --> 00:02:20,320
Elle doit être complètement épuisée.
She must be completely exhausted.

65
00:02:20,420 --> 00:02:22,960
Mais non, mais Isabelle, c'est une force de la nature.
No, no, Isabelle is a force of nature.

66
00:02:23,460 --> 00:02:25,220
Elle a la résistance d'un charpas népalais.
She has the stamina of a Nepalese sherpa.

67
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:26,780
T'inquiète pas.
Don't worry.

68
00:02:37,440 --> 00:02:38,020
Isabelle ?
Isabelle?

69
00:02:43,290 --> 00:02:43,910
Isabelle ?
Isabelle?

70
00:02:46,180 --> 00:02:46,680
Ça va ?
You okay?

71
00:02:46,680 --> 00:02:47,340
Ah, tu m'as fait peur.
Oh, you gave me a fright.

72
00:02:47,640 --> 00:02:48,660
Parce que moi, j'ai...
Because I...

73
00:02:48,700 --> 00:02:49,940
J'ai frappé, mais...
I knocked, but...

74
00:02:49,940 --> 00:02:52,000
T'entendais pas que je le répétais ?
Didn't you hear me calling?

75
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:52,280
Ah, non.
Ah, no.

76
00:02:53,420 --> 00:02:54,520
Ça va, Gabriel ?
You okay, Gabriel?

77
00:02:54,520 --> 00:02:54,920
Très bien.
Very well.

78
00:02:55,840 --> 00:02:58,360
Euh, tu m'excuses une minute, je termine de stabilité.
Um, excuse me a minute, I'm finishing up the stabilization.

79
00:03:00,080 --> 00:03:01,460
Alors, euh...
So, um...

80
00:03:03,960 --> 00:03:05,560
Horatio, reine misérable à Dieu,
Horatio, wretched queen before God,

81
00:03:05,940 --> 00:03:07,880
vous qui m'a laissé trembler devant cette catastrophe,
you who left me trembling before this catastrophe,

82
00:03:08,420 --> 00:03:10,600
j'en avais le temps, mais résignons-nous.
I had the time, but let us resign ourselves.

83
00:03:11,100 --> 00:03:13,840
Horatio, je meurs, vis, meurs,
Horatio, I die, live, die,

84
00:03:13,860 --> 00:03:16,220
justifie-moi, explique ma cause à ceux qui m'ignorent.
vindicate me, explain my cause to those who do not know me.

85
00:03:16,280 --> 00:03:17,700
Mais c'est Marie-Médicis, hein ?
But that's Marie de Medici, right?

86
00:03:17,700 --> 00:03:19,480
Ah, ben non, ça, c'est Hamlet.
Oh no, that's Hamlet.

87
00:03:20,140 --> 00:03:20,300
Ah.
Ah.

88
00:03:23,020 --> 00:03:24,640
Ben, tu sais bien que je jouais Hamlet en mars à l'Odéon.
Well, you know I was playing Hamlet in March at the Odéon.

89
00:03:24,860 --> 00:03:25,840
Mais attends, attends, attends, attends.
Wait, wait, wait, wait.

90
00:03:25,940 --> 00:03:28,120
Tu joues dans Hamlet en mars ?
You're playing in Hamlet in March?

91
00:03:28,120 --> 00:03:29,020
Ah, non, non, non, non.
Oh, no, no, no, no.

92
00:03:29,120 --> 00:03:30,240
Je veux pas dans Hamlet.
I don't want a part in Hamlet.

93
00:03:31,020 --> 00:03:32,120
Je suis Hamlet.
I am Hamlet.

94
00:03:32,780 --> 00:03:33,680
Je joue Hamlet.
I play Hamlet.

95
00:03:34,770 --> 00:03:36,030
Ben, oui, Hamlet, c'est moi.
Well yes, Hamlet — that's me.

96
00:03:36,350 --> 00:03:37,030
Ah, ben, c'est formidable.
Oh, well, that's wonderful.

97
00:03:37,470 --> 00:03:38,530
Ben, oui, c'est formidable.
Well yes, it's wonderful.

98
00:03:39,800 --> 00:03:41,120
Mais t'es sûre que tu nous en as parlé ?
But are you sure you told us about this?

99
00:03:41,120 --> 00:03:42,640
Parce que j'ai pas souvenir de...
Because I don't remember...

100
00:03:42,640 --> 00:03:44,180
Oh, ben, oui, j'aurais pas fait ça dans votre dos.
Oh, of course, I wouldn't have done that behind your backs.

101
00:03:45,640 --> 00:03:46,400
Tu veux un thé ?
Would you like some tea?

102
00:03:47,040 --> 00:03:47,320
Volontiers.
I'd love some.

103
00:03:51,300 --> 00:03:52,540
C'est ça, je me débrouille.
Right, I'll manage.

104
00:03:54,380 --> 00:03:55,340
Et, euh, dis-moi,
And, um, tell me,

105
00:03:55,700 --> 00:03:58,580
t'as pas oublié que tu tournes dans Leclerc-Denis en mars, hein ?
you haven't forgotten you're shooting the Leclerc-Denis in March, have you?

106
00:03:58,580 --> 00:04:01,500
Euh, ben, oui, ben, on s'arrangera, hein.
Um, well yes, we'll work it out.

107
00:04:01,540 --> 00:04:02,340
Le théâtre, c'est le soir.
Theatre is in the evenings.

108
00:04:04,750 --> 00:04:06,190
Écoute, j'allais pas refuser de jouer Hamlet,
Look, I wasn't going to turn down playing Hamlet,

109
00:04:06,230 --> 00:04:08,250
mais en scène par Walikowski, avec...
directed by Walikowski, with...

110
00:04:08,250 --> 00:04:09,530
Comment ça s'appelle, déjà ?
What's her name again?

111
00:04:10,150 --> 00:04:10,430
Euh...
Um...

112
00:04:10,810 --> 00:04:11,490
Qui, ça ?
Who?

113
00:04:11,490 --> 00:04:13,510
La petite, là, qui se promène toujours dans Tokyo, là.
That girl who's always wandering around Tokyo.

114
00:04:14,390 --> 00:04:14,670
Euh...
Um...

115
00:04:14,670 --> 00:04:15,330
Ah !
Ah!

116
00:04:15,330 --> 00:04:16,970
Le film de Sofia Coppola.
The Sofia Coppola film.

117
00:04:17,070 --> 00:04:17,970
Ah, Scarlett Johansson.
Ah, Scarlett Johansson.

118
00:04:17,970 --> 00:04:18,210
Voilà.
That's the one.

119
00:04:18,470 --> 00:04:19,390
Et c'est elle qui va jouer Ophélie.
And she's playing Ophelia.

120
00:04:19,450 --> 00:04:19,890
Vachement bien.
Pretty great.

121
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:21,280
Ouais.
Yeah.

122
00:04:22,670 --> 00:04:23,910
En même temps, j'ai envie de te dire,
At the same time, I have to say,

123
00:04:24,690 --> 00:04:25,710
chaque chose en son temps, hein.
one thing at a time, right.

124
00:04:27,500 --> 00:04:28,200
Sinon, ça va ?
How are you doing anyway?

125
00:04:28,200 --> 00:04:29,880
T'es pas trop crevée, les deux tournages, là ?
Not too wiped out, juggling two shoots?

126
00:04:29,880 --> 00:04:31,320
Je te cache pas, je suis lessivée, hein.
I won't lie, I'm exhausted.

127
00:04:32,620 --> 00:04:34,320
Mais tu vois, je me rends compte que...
But you know, I've realized that...

128
00:04:34,900 --> 00:04:35,680
quand t'arrives...
when you push through...

129
00:04:36,680 --> 00:04:38,720
au-delà de la fatigue, tu bascules dans un état...
beyond the exhaustion, you slip into a state...

130
00:04:39,160 --> 00:04:40,120
Je sais pas comment expliquer.
I don't know how to describe it.

131
00:04:40,980 --> 00:04:41,940
T'es comme une transe.
It's like a trance.

132
00:04:42,560 --> 00:04:44,020
Alors, forcément, c'est très euphorisant.
And naturally, it's very exhilarating.

133
00:04:45,600 --> 00:04:46,060
Forcément, oui.
Naturally, yes.

134
00:04:49,670 --> 00:04:50,590
Tu te drogues ?
Are you on drugs?

135
00:04:50,590 --> 00:04:52,350
Mais non, Gabriel !
Of course not, Gabriel!

136
00:04:53,430 --> 00:04:54,610
C'est de la cortisone.
It's cortisone.

137
00:04:54,670 --> 00:04:55,850
C'est pour mes cordes vocales.
It's for my vocal cords.

138
00:04:58,940 --> 00:04:59,460
Ahem !
Ahem!

139
00:04:59,940 --> 00:05:01,440
Oh, Gabriel, pour qui tu me prends ?
Oh, Gabriel, what do you take me for?

140
00:05:01,740 --> 00:05:03,060
Ma seule drogue, c'est les fruits secs.
My only drug is dried fruit.

141
00:05:03,240 --> 00:05:03,900
T'en veux ?
Want some?

142
00:05:03,900 --> 00:05:04,680
Ah non, merci.
Ah no, thank you.

143
00:05:04,900 --> 00:05:05,380
C'est gentiment...
That's kind of...

144
00:05:05,380 --> 00:05:05,540
C'est gentil.
That's kind.

145
00:05:07,890 --> 00:05:08,610
Yes ?
Yes?

146
00:05:08,610 --> 00:05:10,550
Les affaires, excuse-moi, but don't worry, please.
Business, excuse me, but don't worry, please.

147
00:05:10,590 --> 00:05:11,330
Yes, coming.
Yes, coming.

148
00:05:11,630 --> 00:05:16,630
Mais t'as pas de perruque, là ?
But you don't have a wig on?

149
00:05:16,630 --> 00:05:18,810
Non, tu joues Delphine, dans She's a Femme Fatale.
No, you're playing Delphine in She's a Femme Fatale.

150
00:05:19,010 --> 00:05:19,370
Ah !
Ah!

151
00:05:21,370 --> 00:05:22,410
Delphine, le chapeau.
Delphine, the hat.

152
00:05:24,070 --> 00:05:25,090
Marie, la perruque.
Marie, the wig.

153
00:06:10,040 --> 00:06:11,260
Désolé de t'avoir fait venir ici,
Sorry to drag you out here,

154
00:06:11,320 --> 00:06:13,340
mais je plaide toute la journée, j'aurai pas cinq minutes.
but I'm in court all day, I won't have five minutes.

155
00:06:13,520 --> 00:06:14,240
Je t'en prie.
Please, don't worry about it.

156
00:06:14,980 --> 00:06:16,240
On travaille tous comme des fous.
We're all working like crazy.

157
00:06:17,320 --> 00:06:19,200
La semaine dernière, on a réussi par miracle
Last week, we somehow managed

158
00:06:19,200 --> 00:06:20,720
à dîner avec Emmanuel et les Perrenemann.
to have dinner with Emmanuel and the Perrenemanns.

159
00:06:20,860 --> 00:06:21,220
Ah !
Ah!

160
00:06:21,660 --> 00:06:22,580
Comment vont-ils ?
How are they?

161
00:06:22,580 --> 00:06:23,120
Bien, bien.
Good, good.

162
00:06:23,640 --> 00:06:24,900
Et Catherine ?
And Catherine?

163
00:06:25,320 --> 00:06:26,580
Ça va, je te remercie.
She's fine, thank you for asking.

164
00:06:26,900 --> 00:06:27,320
Tant mieux.
Glad to hear it.

165
00:06:28,660 --> 00:06:30,220
Et chez ASK, alors, comment ça se passe
And at ASK, how have things been

166
00:06:30,220 --> 00:06:31,360
depuis le décès de Samuel ?
since Samuel passed away?

167
00:06:32,920 --> 00:06:33,700
Ah, ça a été...
Ah, it's been...

168
00:06:35,360 --> 00:06:35,680
mouvementé.
turbulent.

169
00:06:37,480 --> 00:06:39,020
On a fini par trouver un repreneur.
We eventually found a buyer.

170
00:06:39,920 --> 00:06:41,320
Enfin, moi, j'étais pas vraiment pour,
Honestly, I wasn't really in favor of it,

171
00:06:41,380 --> 00:06:43,840
mais j'ai pas eu trop le choix.
but I didn't have much of a choice.

172
00:06:43,940 --> 00:06:45,380
Comme tu sais, je me suis pas tout seul.
As you know, I'm not on my own there.

173
00:06:47,320 --> 00:06:49,020
Mais bon, les talents sont restés,
But the talent stayed on,

174
00:06:49,580 --> 00:06:51,640
les projets s'enchaînent, c'est l'essentiel.
projects keep coming in — that's what matters.

175
00:06:53,460 --> 00:06:54,100
Écoute, Mathias,
Listen, Mathias,

176
00:06:55,870 --> 00:06:58,510
c'est pas très déontologique de ma part,
this isn't very ethical of me,

177
00:06:58,590 --> 00:07:00,350
mais on se connaît depuis 30 ans,
but we've known each other for 30 years —

178
00:07:00,730 --> 00:07:02,250
je ne peux pas ne rien te dire.
I can't say nothing.

179
00:07:03,420 --> 00:07:04,560
Il se passe des choses...
Things are happening...

180
00:07:04,560 --> 00:07:05,500
dans ton agence.
inside your agency.

181
00:07:08,810 --> 00:07:09,870
C'est Janowski ?
Is that Janowski?

182
00:07:10,450 --> 00:07:10,770
Non.
No.

183
00:07:12,010 --> 00:07:13,110
D'autres collaborateurs.
Other associates.

184
00:07:13,600 --> 00:07:14,460
Tu devrais te méfier.
You should watch your back.

185
00:07:20,400 --> 00:07:21,300
Andréa Martel ?
Andréa Martel?

186
00:07:21,300 --> 00:07:25,360
Je peux rien te dire.
I can't tell you anything.

187
00:07:27,160 --> 00:07:27,800
Elle va partir.
She's leaving.

188
00:07:30,010 --> 00:07:32,110
À ta place, j'assurerai mes arrières.
If I were you, I'd cover myself.

189
00:07:33,210 --> 00:07:33,650
Voilà tout.
That's all.

190
00:07:40,370 --> 00:07:40,970
Merci, Charles.
Thank you, Charles.

191
00:07:54,930 --> 00:07:55,790
C'est génial pour nous.
This is great for us.

192
00:07:55,910 --> 00:07:56,810
C'est l'origine des projets,
They're where projects come from,

193
00:07:56,910 --> 00:07:57,850
et en plus, ils sont quand même
and on top of that, they're still

194
00:07:57,850 --> 00:07:59,630
vachement plus faciles à gérer que les acteurs.
way easier to deal with than actors.

195
00:08:00,050 --> 00:08:01,630
Ouais, mais qu'est-ce qui s'habille mal ?
Yeah, but the fashion sense — painful.

196
00:08:01,630 --> 00:08:03,560
C'est douloureux, un rendez-vous,
A meeting can be rough,

197
00:08:03,600 --> 00:08:04,720
j'ai parfois du mal à les écouter.
I sometimes struggle to listen to them.

198
00:08:06,390 --> 00:08:08,870
Et sinon, c'est la saison des présentations d'atelier
Otherwise, it's workshop showcase season

199
00:08:08,870 --> 00:08:10,030
dans les écoles de théâtre.
at the theater schools.

200
00:08:10,910 --> 00:08:12,310
Une répartition aléatoire entre nous.
We split them randomly among ourselves.

201
00:08:14,480 --> 00:08:15,220
Moi, pas du tout.
Not me, not at all.

202
00:08:15,400 --> 00:08:15,920
Ah bah si, attends.
Oh come on, yes you do.

203
00:08:16,320 --> 00:08:18,060
Non, le conservatoire, c'est pas négociable.
No, the conservatoire is non-negotiable.

204
00:08:18,200 --> 00:08:19,860
J'ai un de mes acteurs qui y est, je suis obligée.
One of my actors is there, I have to go.

205
00:08:20,240 --> 00:08:21,760
Toi, tu peux aller à l'atelier de scène ?
Can you take the stage workshop?

206
00:08:21,760 --> 00:08:22,540
C'est une très bonne école.
It's a very good school.

207
00:08:22,700 --> 00:08:24,620
Je sais, mais je peux pas, c'est dans le 20e.
I know, but I can't — it's in the 20th.

208
00:08:24,880 --> 00:08:25,640
Quoi ? Pourquoi ?
What? Why?

209
00:08:25,640 --> 00:08:27,160
J'aime pas les arrondissements à deux chiffres,
I don't like two-digit arrondissements,

210
00:08:27,180 --> 00:08:27,600
c'est trop loin.
it's too far.

211
00:08:28,290 --> 00:08:29,870
Non, attends, si tu veux être Camille Valentini,
No, wait — if you want to be Camille Valentini,

212
00:08:29,970 --> 00:08:30,710
tu peux pas être aussi snob.
you can't be that much of a snob.

213
00:08:31,290 --> 00:08:31,570
Bonjour.
Hello.

214
00:08:32,820 --> 00:08:33,100
Bonjour.
Hello.

215
00:08:38,900 --> 00:08:40,460
Vous interrompez pas pour moi, continuez.
Don't stop on my account, carry on.

216
00:08:42,650 --> 00:08:44,490
C'est vrai qu'elle est belle, cette plante,
That is a beautiful plant,

217
00:08:44,670 --> 00:08:47,230
mais après, elle boit beaucoup.
though it does drink a lot.

218
00:08:47,830 --> 00:08:51,870
C'est quoi, ça, Mathieu ?
What's that, Mathieu?

219
00:08:51,890 --> 00:08:52,970
C'est une fougère ?
Is it a fern?

220
00:08:54,670 --> 00:08:55,550
Je ne sais pas.
I don't know.

221
00:09:11,580 --> 00:09:13,800
L'agence, c'est ma deuxième famille.
The agency is my second family.

222
00:09:15,130 --> 00:09:17,730
Et toi, toi, tu es ma famille dans cette famille.
And you — you are my family within that family.

223
00:09:19,870 --> 00:09:22,440
Ah ouais ? Et donc ?
Oh yeah? So?

224
00:09:22,440 --> 00:09:23,980
Je supporterai pas contre Aïs.
I won't side against Aïs.

225
00:09:25,790 --> 00:09:26,970
Je vois pas pourquoi tu dis ça.
I don't see why you'd say that.

226
00:09:29,340 --> 00:09:30,740
Si quoi que ce soit se préparer
If anything is being planned

227
00:09:30,740 --> 00:09:31,780
qu'il puisse mettre l'agence en danger,
that could put the agency at risk,

228
00:09:31,920 --> 00:09:32,520
tu me préviendrais.
you'd warn me.

229
00:09:33,380 --> 00:09:33,920
Bien sûr.
Of course.

230
00:09:34,500 --> 00:09:36,080
Parce que tu vois, tu es ma fille,
Because you see, you're my daughter,

231
00:09:36,180 --> 00:09:37,460
et ça, c'est plus important que tout.
and that matters more than anything.

232
00:09:38,020 --> 00:09:39,360
Il faut que je puisse avoir confiance en toi.
I need to be able to trust you.

233
00:09:39,800 --> 00:09:40,420
Oui, évidemment.
Yes, obviously.

234
00:09:41,500 --> 00:09:42,280
Mais tout va bien.
But everything's fine.

235
00:09:43,090 --> 00:09:43,530
Je te préviens.
I'm letting you know.

236
00:09:45,940 --> 00:09:48,220
Je peux y aller ? Pardon, mais j'ai plein de boulot, là.
Can I go? Sorry, but I've got a ton of work right now.

237
00:09:48,380 --> 00:09:48,640
Oui, oui.
Yes, yes.

238
00:09:48,820 --> 00:09:50,020
Avec le congé, maintenant, je vais...
With the leave now, I'm going to…

239
00:09:58,910 --> 00:10:00,230
Voilà, c'est dans la mémoire.
There we go, it's in the system.

240
00:10:00,390 --> 00:10:04,100
On peut pas marcher sur la tâche de l'accouchement,
We can't step on the birth task,

241
00:10:04,140 --> 00:10:04,780
c'est au-delà de mes forces.
It's beyond me.

242
00:10:08,740 --> 00:10:09,480
Je crois qu'il se doute.
I think he suspects something.

243
00:10:10,060 --> 00:10:12,040
Comment ça, tu crois ? Il t'a dit quoi, exactement ?
What do you mean, you think? What did he say, exactly?

244
00:10:12,040 --> 00:10:13,080
C'était pas très précis.
It wasn't very specific.

245
00:10:13,730 --> 00:10:15,310
Il a dit qu'il supporterait pas contre Aïs
He said he couldn't stand being against Aïs

246
00:10:15,670 --> 00:10:18,070
et que je devais absolument lui dire
and that I absolutely had to tell him

247
00:10:18,070 --> 00:10:19,910
si je sentais que quelque chose pouvait faire du mal à l'agence.
if I felt something could hurt the agency.

248
00:10:20,370 --> 00:10:21,510
Ah, OK, c'est bon, il sait rien.
Oh, OK, it's fine, he doesn't know anything.

249
00:10:22,800 --> 00:10:23,660
Comment ça ?
What do you mean?

250
00:10:23,660 --> 00:10:25,660
C'est pas le genre à tourner autour du pot.
He's not the type to beat around the bush.

251
00:10:25,820 --> 00:10:27,540
S'il était au courant, il aurait déjà déshérité.
If he knew, he'd have already cut me out of the will.

252
00:10:28,240 --> 00:10:29,760
Pourquoi il m'a dit tout ça, alors ?
So why did he say all that to me, then?

253
00:10:29,760 --> 00:10:31,040
J'en sais rien, moi.
I have no idea.

254
00:10:31,200 --> 00:10:32,320
C'est un grand parano, ton père.
Your father's a serious paranoid.

255
00:10:33,060 --> 00:10:35,100
Quand il y a plus de café, je crois que c'est dirigé contre lui.
When the coffee runs out, he thinks it's a personal attack.

256
00:10:35,640 --> 00:10:42,780
Je suis une assez lancoume.
I'm kind of a mess.

257
00:10:55,550 --> 00:10:56,130
Salut, Kini.
Hey, Kini.

258
00:10:57,190 --> 00:10:58,670
Ah, je te laisse finir ?
Oh, should I let you finish?

259
00:10:58,670 --> 00:10:59,830
T'es pas obligée de répondre ?
You don't have to answer?

260
00:10:59,830 --> 00:11:01,790
Si, je vais pas disparaître du jour au lendemain.
I will — I'm not going to vanish overnight.

261
00:11:02,070 --> 00:11:02,610
Mais si.
Oh, but you might.

262
00:11:02,970 --> 00:11:04,650
Non, je peux pas me permettre de perdre le Kini.
No, I can't afford to lose Kini.

263
00:11:07,160 --> 00:11:10,700
Allô ? Fabrice, ça va ? Tu vas bien ?
Hello? Fabrice, you okay? Everything alright?

264
00:11:11,280 --> 00:11:12,780
Ah, merci, c'est gentil.
Oh, thanks, that's sweet.

265
00:11:12,780 --> 00:11:13,640
Bah, écoute, c'est super.
Well, listen, that's great.

266
00:11:13,860 --> 00:11:15,180
La petite est vraiment...
The little one is really...

267
00:11:15,800 --> 00:11:20,490
Ah, si, si, si, normalement,
Oh, yes, yes, normally,

268
00:11:20,510 --> 00:11:21,130
ton chien est habillé.
your dog is dressed.

269
00:11:21,250 --> 00:11:22,630
Déjà, moi, ça, c'est vu avec la prod.
That part, I've already sorted with production.

270
00:11:23,190 --> 00:11:26,110
Ah, d'accord, bah, alors ça, il faudrait voir avec mon assistante.
Oh, right, well, you'd need to take that up with my assistant.

271
00:11:27,240 --> 00:11:28,320
Non, elle est très bien.
No, she's great.

272
00:11:28,460 --> 00:11:29,360
Ouh là là, t'inquiète pas.
Oh, don't you worry.

273
00:11:29,380 --> 00:11:31,720
Bonjour. La pommade anti-hémorroïdaire.
Hello. The hemorrhoid cream.

274
00:11:31,960 --> 00:11:32,820
Je la pose là ?
Should I put it here?

275
00:11:32,820 --> 00:11:34,120
Ça va, ça se passe bien ?
How's it going, everything okay?

276
00:11:34,120 --> 00:11:36,580
Oui, oui, elle a bien pris, c'est bon.
Yes, yes, it's taken well, we're good.

277
00:11:36,820 --> 00:11:37,980
Et vous êtes allée à la selle ?
And have you had a bowel movement?

278
00:11:39,980 --> 00:11:41,840
Euh... Non, pardon, c'est pas moi, c'est elle.
Uh... No, sorry, not me — her.

279
00:11:42,020 --> 00:11:43,020
Ah oui, pardon, d'accord.
Oh yes, sorry, of course.

280
00:11:43,280 --> 00:11:45,420
Oui, c'est vous, les deux mamans.
Right, you're both mothers.

281
00:11:45,620 --> 00:11:46,780
Oui, on m'a dit, mais j'avais oublié.
Yes, I was told, but I forgot.

282
00:11:47,040 --> 00:11:49,460
Ça se passe bien, du coup, vous êtes allée à la selle ?
So how's it going — have you had a bowel movement?

283
00:11:49,460 --> 00:11:51,100
Ah, non, Fabrice,
Oh no, Fabrice,

284
00:11:51,100 --> 00:11:53,160
Fabrice, pardon, je peux te rappeler ?
Fabrice, sorry, can I call you back?

285
00:11:53,160 --> 00:11:53,860
Là, j'ai un imprévu.
Something's come up.

286
00:11:56,160 --> 00:11:56,840
Euh... Toujours pas.
Uh... Still nothing.

287
00:11:57,140 --> 00:11:57,420
Non.
No.

288
00:12:00,090 --> 00:12:04,020
Dis-moi, tu veux pas lui lâcher un peu l'abri de la Gabrielle ?
Listen, don't you think you could give Gabrielle a little more breathing room?

289
00:12:04,440 --> 00:12:05,940
Quand il aura mis de l'ordre dans son bordel,
When he's got his act together,

290
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:07,300
je le lâcherai. Pour l'instant, j'ai pas confiance.
I'll ease up. For now, I don't trust him.

291
00:12:08,230 --> 00:12:09,810
Tu vois, moi, mon chien, mon Jean-Gabin,
You know, my dog, my Jean-Gabin —

292
00:12:10,310 --> 00:12:11,550
quand je lui mets la laisse trop court,
when I keep the leash too short,

293
00:12:11,910 --> 00:12:14,330
ça l'énerve. Alors il s'excite, il aboie,
it winds him up. He gets agitated, he barks,

294
00:12:14,730 --> 00:12:15,790
il a qu'une envie, c'est de mordre.
all he wants to do is bite.

295
00:12:16,050 --> 00:12:18,080
Ah bah, ça lui ferait pas de mal à Gabrielle
Well, it wouldn't hurt Gabrielle

296
00:12:18,080 --> 00:12:18,940
d'avoir un peu envie de mordre.
to want to bite a little.

297
00:12:19,240 --> 00:12:21,080
Jusqu'au moment où il bouffe sa laisse et il part en courant.
Until the day he chews through the leash and takes off running.

298
00:12:22,750 --> 00:12:23,430
Fais gaffe, Hicham.
Watch yourself, Hicham.

299
00:12:23,430 --> 00:12:25,940
Hicham, si tu lui donnes pas un peu de mou,
Hicham, if you don't give him some slack,

300
00:12:26,930 --> 00:12:28,330
tu pourrais très vite te retrouver tout seul.
you could find yourself very alone, very fast.

301
00:12:28,730 --> 00:12:30,850
Pourquoi pas une seconde ?
Why not a second?

302
00:12:31,310 --> 00:12:32,990
Quoi ? Qu'il pourrait avoir envie de partir ?
What? That he might want to leave?

303
00:12:35,420 --> 00:12:39,980
C'est pas le genre. Je sais pas, il aurait pas le courage, non ?
Not his style. I don't know, he wouldn't have the guts, would he?

304
00:12:40,540 --> 00:12:41,020
Peut-être.
Maybe.

305
00:12:42,090 --> 00:12:44,140
Peut-être pas. Si j'étais toi,
Maybe not. If I were you,

306
00:12:44,200 --> 00:12:44,760
je t'en ferais pas le diable.
I wouldn't make a devil out of him.

307
00:12:46,190 --> 00:12:49,780
Gabrielle ? Tu sais, on parlait de toi, justement, là.
Gabrielle? You know, we were just talking about you.

308
00:12:50,080 --> 00:12:50,660
Ah ! Ouais.
Oh! Yeah.

309
00:12:51,360 --> 00:12:53,600
On se disait que s'il y avait bien quelqu'un qui tenait à escasse, c'était toi.
We were saying that if anyone was hanging on by a thread, it was you.

310
00:12:55,220 --> 00:12:55,700
Ah, tellement.
Oh, completely.

311
00:12:56,280 --> 00:12:59,750
Ah, j'ai vu Isabelle Hyper hier soir.
I saw Isabelle Hyper last night.

312
00:13:00,270 --> 00:13:01,110
Elle va super.
She's doing great.

313
00:13:01,510 --> 00:13:03,350
Ça va passer comme une autre à la poste, ce petit chevauchement, là.
This little overlap will blow over like any other, don't worry.

314
00:13:03,770 --> 00:13:04,770
Bah, t'es en pleine forme.
Well, you're in great shape.

315
00:13:07,320 --> 00:13:08,730
Bonjour. Je veux voir Gabrielle.
Hello. I'd like to see Gabrielle.

316
00:13:09,050 --> 00:13:11,020
Elle est pas dans son bureau.
She's not in her office.

317
00:13:11,980 --> 00:13:14,220
Ah, ben voilà. Qu'est-ce qui se passe ?
Right. So what's going on?

318
00:13:14,990 --> 00:13:17,490
Eh ben, il se passe que les Américains ont modifié le plan de travail.
Well, the Americans have changed the shooting schedule.

319
00:13:17,710 --> 00:13:19,570
Ils veulent qu'on retourne des scènes de nuit en extérieur.
They want us to reshoot some night scenes on location.

320
00:13:19,890 --> 00:13:21,290
Mais moi, cette nuit, je tourne avec Cédric.
But tonight I'm shooting with Cédric.

321
00:13:22,410 --> 00:13:24,210
C'est pas possible. Qu'est-ce qu'on fait ?
That's not possible. What do we do?

322
00:13:24,550 --> 00:13:25,470
Viens, on va se mettre dans mon bureau.
Come on, let's go to my office.

323
00:13:25,630 --> 00:13:26,790
Un jour, c'est ce que vous voulez ?
One day — is that what you want?

324
00:13:26,790 --> 00:13:27,790
Dites-moi où je t'ai dit.
Tell me where I told you.

325
00:13:29,720 --> 00:13:32,740
Pardon, je te parle comme ça.
Sorry, I'm being blunt with you.

326
00:13:33,020 --> 00:13:34,400
Non, mais t'inquiète. T'as bien fait.
No, don't worry. You did the right thing.

327
00:13:36,470 --> 00:13:44,960
Ah, mais t'as pas la même photo de moi ?
Oh, don't you have a different photo of me?

328
00:13:46,520 --> 00:13:46,880
Ah, non.
No.

329
00:13:47,870 --> 00:13:48,430
Tiens, c'est vrai.
Oh, right, fair enough.

330
00:13:48,810 --> 00:13:57,050
Bon, qu'est-ce qu'on fait, alors ?
So, what do we do then?

331
00:13:57,050 --> 00:14:02,590
Eh ben, écoute, le problème, c'est que les Américains, côté droit, ils sont assez tatillons.
Well, look, the problem is the Americans — on the rights side, they can be pretty nitpicky.

332
00:14:02,990 --> 00:14:05,330
Il faudrait bien qu'ils comprennent que parfois, le désir, c'est plus fort que le droit.
They need to understand that sometimes desire is stronger than the law.

333
00:14:05,550 --> 00:14:06,370
Oui, d'accord.
Yes, sure.

334
00:14:07,030 --> 00:14:08,570
Je suis pas certain que ça puisse suffire, ça.
I'm not sure that's going to be enough.

335
00:14:09,030 --> 00:14:10,330
Mais écoute, Gabrielle, ils me connaissent.
But listen, Gabrielle, they know me.

336
00:14:11,030 --> 00:14:13,430
Quand je me retrouve la même année avec quatre films sélectionnés à Cannes,
When I end up in the same year with four films selected at Cannes,

337
00:14:13,450 --> 00:14:15,090
c'est bien qu'il y a eu des petits chevauchements, non ?
it's because there were a few overlaps, isn't it?

338
00:14:15,090 --> 00:14:16,690
Oui, c'est bien, bien sûr, mais...
Yes, that's true, of course, but...

339
00:14:18,080 --> 00:14:19,180
Écoute, tu sais quoi ?
Look, you know what?

340
00:14:19,180 --> 00:14:21,260
On va s'arranger avec l'équipe française.
We'll work it out with the French crew.

341
00:14:21,500 --> 00:14:23,560
Voilà, on va leur expliquer que de toute façon, tu peux pas tourner cette nuit,
We'll explain that you simply can't shoot tonight —

342
00:14:25,980 --> 00:14:27,280
tu penses bien que j'ai tâté le terrain.
you know I've already tested the waters.

343
00:14:27,440 --> 00:14:30,700
Le problème, c'est qu'ils ont loué un hôtel particulier que ça leur coûte atrocement cher
The problem is they've rented a private mansion and it's costing them a fortune,

344
00:14:30,700 --> 00:14:32,760
et qu'ils peuvent pas le garder plusieurs jours.
and they can't keep it for several days.

345
00:14:32,860 --> 00:14:34,140
Donc on est obligés de tourner cette nuit.
So we have no choice but to shoot tonight.

346
00:14:36,380 --> 00:14:37,500
Non, je te dis, c'est la tuile.
I'm telling you, it's a nightmare.

347
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:40,620
Oui, et puis sur le front des Américains, on a zéro ouverture, là.
And on the American front, we have zero room to maneuver.

348
00:14:41,080 --> 00:14:42,540
Bon, ben, pas de panique.
Okay, don't panic.

349
00:14:42,620 --> 00:14:44,280
Regardez, à Bollywood, ils tournent bien six films par jour.
Look, in Bollywood they shoot six films a day.

350
00:14:44,460 --> 00:14:46,380
Nous, on devrait bien pouvoir caser deux tournages en une nuit.
We should be able to squeeze in two shoots in one night.

351
00:14:46,660 --> 00:14:47,800
Oui, mais enfin...
Yes, but still...

352
00:14:49,180 --> 00:14:50,980
Allez, Gabrielle, ça va s'arranger.
Come on, Gabrielle, it'll work out.

353
00:14:51,420 --> 00:14:53,700
Avec toi, ça arrange toujours, non ?
With you, it always does, doesn't it?

354
00:14:53,700 --> 00:14:59,650
Tiens, y a encore une photo de ce style de France ?
Wait, is there another photo like that from France?

355
00:15:00,580 --> 00:15:02,960
T'as de la chance qu'on soit dans la mer, parce que ça pourrait m'énerver, hein.
Lucky for you we're in the water, or that could really get on my nerves.

356
00:15:05,700 --> 00:15:07,100
Pour Flora, avec nos meilleurs sentiments.
For Flora, with our warmest regards.

357
00:15:07,860 --> 00:15:08,960
Mathias, c'est pour un bébé.
Mathias, this is for a baby.

358
00:15:10,630 --> 00:15:11,810
Vous voulez pas le faire, vous ?
Don't you want to do it yourself?

359
00:15:11,810 --> 00:15:13,190
Ah non, alors là, sûrement pas.
Oh no, absolutely not.

360
00:15:13,880 --> 00:15:15,340
Vous avez un cœur, servez-vous-en.
You have a heart — use it.

361
00:15:19,650 --> 00:15:21,610
Et puis dépêchez-vous, je dois aller à la maternité.
And hurry up, I need to get to the maternity ward.

362
00:15:28,940 --> 00:15:30,500
Vous pensez pas du tout au bébé, là.
You're not thinking about the baby at all right now.

363
00:15:33,100 --> 00:15:36,900
Mathias, l'expérience nous a prouvé qu'il valait mieux ne pas tout mélanger.
Mathias, experience has taught us it's better not to mix everything together.

364
00:15:37,600 --> 00:15:37,920
Oui.
Yes.

365
00:15:38,480 --> 00:15:39,120
Restons concentrés.
Let's stay focused.

366
00:15:46,070 --> 00:15:48,310
Pour la petite Flora, notre bébé a ESCA.
For little Flora, our baby has ESCA.

367
00:15:48,510 --> 00:15:50,210
