544
00:24:50,510 --> 00:24:51,030
Peut-être pas.
Maybe not.

545
00:24:51,700 --> 00:24:54,340
Tu sais que Noémie a un don pour les plans de travail incompatibles.
You know Noémie has a gift for making incompatible schedules work.

546
00:24:54,420 --> 00:24:55,060
Elle est incroyable.
She's incredible.

547
00:24:55,460 --> 00:24:57,080
Elle peut faire rentrer des ronds dans des carrés.
She can fit round pegs into square holes.

548
00:24:57,220 --> 00:24:58,800
Elle m'a sauvé des coups, tu n'as même pas idée.
She's saved me so many times, you have no idea.

549
00:24:58,960 --> 00:24:59,560
Ah bon ?
Oh really?

550
00:25:01,160 --> 00:25:03,400
Prends une heure, on voit si ça marche, et puis sinon, on avise.
Take an hour, we see if it works, and if not, we figure something out.

551
00:25:03,660 --> 00:25:05,020
Mais tu n'as pas les trucs à faire, toi ?
But don't you have things to do?

552
00:25:05,020 --> 00:25:06,140
Si, si, mais ça ne fait rien, ce n'est pas important.
Yes, yes, but never mind, it's not important.

553
00:25:07,320 --> 00:25:08,700
Mathias, ça va ?
Mathias, you okay?

554
00:25:08,700 --> 00:25:09,340
Très bien, oui.
Very well, yes.

555
00:25:12,880 --> 00:25:14,660
Ne sois pas désobligeant non plus, Gabriel.
Don't be rude either, Gabriel.

556
00:25:15,000 --> 00:25:16,660
Je te dis que j'ai envie de t'aider, j'ai envie de t'aider.
I'm telling you I want to help you, I want to help you.

557
00:25:17,760 --> 00:25:18,000
Merci.
Thank you.

558
00:25:18,280 --> 00:25:18,720
Mais de rien.
Don't mention it.

559
00:25:18,940 --> 00:25:19,400
C'est normal.
It's nothing.

560
00:25:19,820 --> 00:25:21,760
C'est important d'être solidaire dans les moments difficiles.
It's important to stick together in difficult times.

561
00:25:21,980 --> 00:25:31,500
Ça va comme ça ?
Is that good?

562
00:25:31,500 --> 00:25:32,380
Oui, c'est parfait.
Yes, perfect.

563
00:25:32,780 --> 00:25:34,340
Et je veux bien un petit café, s'il vous plaît.
And I'd love a little coffee, please.

564
00:25:34,740 --> 00:25:35,580
Avec un peu de lait.
With a bit of milk.

565
00:25:36,000 --> 00:25:36,980
Je vous apporte ça tout de suite.
I'll bring that right away.

566
00:25:39,980 --> 00:25:41,880
Non, mais Gabriel, tu salis tout.
No, but Gabriel, you're making a mess of everything.

567
00:25:41,880 --> 00:25:42,920
Regarde la feuille de service.
Look at the call sheet.

568
00:25:44,340 --> 00:25:44,660
Parlons.
Let's talk.

569
00:25:44,960 --> 00:25:46,360
Pas vrai ?
Right?

570
00:25:46,360 --> 00:25:46,380
Oui.
Yes.

571
00:25:50,530 --> 00:25:54,370
Ah, ça fait 4,6 km entre les deux tournages.
Ah, it's 4.6 km between the two shoots.

572
00:25:54,410 --> 00:25:55,510
Je suis à 25 minutes en voiture.
I'm 25 minutes away by car.

573
00:25:56,270 --> 00:25:57,610
Ça va, c'est un peu le père, ça.
That's not too bad, really.

574
00:25:57,910 --> 00:26:00,350
Oui, sauf qu'il va falloir passer dans le marais.
Yes, except we'll have to go through the Marais.

575
00:26:00,410 --> 00:26:02,290
Ça va être la fin de la pierre, ça peut bouchonner.
It's going to be a nightmare, it could get backed up.

576
00:26:02,350 --> 00:26:03,330
Surtout que jeudi, il y a plein de monde.
Especially on Thursdays, it's packed.

577
00:26:03,370 --> 00:26:04,290
C'est le nouveau samedi, tu sais.
It's the new Saturday, you know.

578
00:26:04,490 --> 00:26:05,030
Chut !
Shh!

579
00:26:10,060 --> 00:26:11,760
Regarde, par contre, là, ici, on est vite.
Look, on the other hand, right here, we're fast.

580
00:26:12,900 --> 00:26:13,600
Ça y est.
That's it.

581
00:26:14,250 --> 00:26:16,250
Je crois que j'ai trouvé un trou dans le marais de Médicis.
I think I found a gap in the Médicis marsh.

582
00:26:16,670 --> 00:26:17,270
Vas-y, balance.
Go on, let's hear it.

583
00:26:19,700 --> 00:26:21,980
Il faut qu'Isabelle demande à Cédric Kahn
Isabelle needs to ask Cédric Kahn

584
00:26:22,400 --> 00:26:23,000
de commander le café.
to order the coffee.

585
00:26:23,020 --> 00:26:24,120
On va commencer par la scène de l'agonie.
We'll start with the death scene.

586
00:26:24,860 --> 00:26:27,360
Là, elle doit tout donner pour pas que ça dure trop longtemps.
She has to give everything so it doesn't drag on too long.

587
00:26:27,560 --> 00:26:28,440
Ça, elle sait le faire, ça.
She knows how to do that.

588
00:26:29,320 --> 00:26:31,360
Après, c'est la scène de la veillée mortuaire.
After that, it's the wake scene.

589
00:26:31,620 --> 00:26:33,820
Donc, par définition, elle est morte.
So by definition, she's dead.

590
00:26:34,820 --> 00:26:37,780
Donc, elle peut exiger d'être remplacée par une doublure.
So she can insist on being replaced by a stand-in.

591
00:26:39,520 --> 00:26:40,880
Contractuellement, elle a le droit de l'exiger.
Contractually, she has the right to demand it.

592
00:26:41,240 --> 00:26:41,560
Absolument.
Absolutely.

593
00:26:42,100 --> 00:26:42,420
OK.
OK.

594
00:26:43,420 --> 00:26:45,140
Donc là, elle dit à Cédric,
So she tells Cédric,

595
00:26:46,080 --> 00:26:48,560
écoute, là, je viens de crever quand même dans d'atroces souffrances.
look, I just died in absolute agony.

596
00:26:48,560 --> 00:26:50,260
J'ai tout donné, je suis épuisée.
I gave everything, I'm exhausted.

597
00:26:50,480 --> 00:26:52,240
Il faut que j'aille me reposer après ma mort.
I need to go rest after my death.

598
00:26:52,480 --> 00:26:53,480
Elle va s'isoler dans le café.
She goes off on her own to the café.

599
00:26:53,500 --> 00:26:53,920
Cédric commence à loger.
Cédric starts blocking the scene.

600
00:26:54,500 --> 00:26:57,360
Là, ça nous ouvre une brèche de trois heures.
That gives us a three-hour window.

601
00:26:58,140 --> 00:27:01,380
Avant la dernière scène avec la confidente dans les jardins.
Before the last scene with the confidante in the gardens.

602
00:27:01,560 --> 00:27:04,640
Et là, ça laisse pile poil le temps de foncer sur les quêtes saines
And that leaves just enough time to rush through the wholesome quests

603
00:27:04,640 --> 00:27:05,640
pour rejoindre les Amerlocs.
to join the Americans.

604
00:27:06,760 --> 00:27:07,900
Je te l'avais dit.
I told you so.

605
00:27:09,510 --> 00:27:10,590
Merci, c'est génial.
Thank you, that's brilliant.

606
00:27:10,610 --> 00:27:11,630
Merci, Noémie, merci.
Thank you, Noémie, thank you.

607
00:27:12,110 --> 00:27:13,610
La reine du plan de travail, merci.
The queen of organization, thank you.

608
00:27:13,870 --> 00:27:14,450
Je vous en prie.
You're welcome.

609
00:27:14,950 --> 00:27:15,390
Pardon.
Excuse me.

610
00:27:15,770 --> 00:27:17,650
Je vous laisse prévenir Isabelle.
I'll let you inform Isabelle.

611
00:27:26,540 --> 00:27:27,400
Bon, j'y vais.
Right, I'm off.

612
00:27:30,490 --> 00:27:33,010
Et vous allez faire quoi avec Hubert ?
And what are you going to do about Hubert?

613
00:27:33,010 --> 00:27:34,170
La Formule 1 ?
Formula 1?

614
00:27:34,170 --> 00:27:35,810
Écoute, je suis désolé.
Look, I'm sorry.

615
00:27:36,700 --> 00:27:37,740
C'est un cas de force majeure.
It's a case of force majeure.

616
00:27:37,800 --> 00:27:39,500
Je me suis engagé auprès de Gabrielle.
I made a commitment to Gabrielle.

617
00:27:40,200 --> 00:27:41,760
C'est très important pour moi, pour l'agence.
It's very important to me, to the agency.

618
00:27:41,900 --> 00:27:42,640
Oui, ne te fatigue pas.
Yeah, don't bother.

619
00:27:42,940 --> 00:27:43,700
J'ai l'habitude.
I'm used to it.

620
00:27:44,180 --> 00:27:48,760
Ne t'inquiète pas, ça va très bien se passer sans toi.
Don't worry, it'll go just fine without you.

621
00:27:50,100 --> 00:27:50,860
Et ce n'est pas plus mal.
And that's not necessarily a bad thing.

622
00:27:50,920 --> 00:27:52,120
Noémie sera beaucoup plus à l'aise aussi.
Noémie will be much more comfortable too.

623
00:27:52,380 --> 00:28:14,100
Même moi, alors.
Even me, then.

624
00:28:15,660 --> 00:28:18,340
Ah, mais vous êtes Alexandre, le kiné ?
Oh, are you Alexandre, the physio?

625
00:28:18,340 --> 00:28:19,020
Oui, oui, oui.
Yes, yes, yes.

626
00:28:19,060 --> 00:28:21,080
Et vous, vous êtes Noémie, la chamenne ?
And you must be Noémie, the expectant mother?

627
00:28:21,380 --> 00:28:22,180
Oui, c'est ça.
Yes, that's right.

628
00:28:24,060 --> 00:28:24,340
Enchanté.
Delighted.

629
00:28:24,540 --> 00:28:26,460
Et votre dos, ça va ? Pas trop mal ?
And your back, how is it? Not too bad?

630
00:28:27,320 --> 00:28:30,300
Ça va, mais c'est surtout l'année que c'est difficile.
It's okay, but it's mostly this time of year that's hard.

631
00:28:30,540 --> 00:28:33,260
Parce que d'habitude, j'aime bien dormir en position fœtale.
Because normally I like to sleep in the fetal position.

632
00:28:33,320 --> 00:28:35,700
Et là, ce n'est pas trop possible.
And right now, that's not really possible.

633
00:28:36,000 --> 00:28:36,580
Oui, c'est bien.
Yes, that makes sense.

634
00:28:36,740 --> 00:28:38,440
Est-ce que vous voulez que je vous montre une vidéo ?
Would you like me to show you a video?

635
00:28:39,560 --> 00:28:40,700
Oui, avec plaisir.
Yes, I'd love that.

636
00:28:42,000 --> 00:28:44,080
Mais là, je n'ai pas toute conscience de mon volume.
But right now I don't have a full sense of my own size.

637
00:29:10,340 --> 00:29:12,040
Je te pardonne, mon enfant.
I forgive you, my child.

638
00:29:14,850 --> 00:29:16,290
Ah, ma jambe.
Ah, my leg.

639
00:29:18,130 --> 00:29:21,050
Vous allez couper ma jambe.
You're going to cut off my leg.

640
00:29:21,330 --> 00:29:24,180
Non, soyez sans crainte.
No, have no fear.

641
00:29:31,010 --> 00:29:33,580
Henri, je te vois.
Henri, I see you.

642
00:29:37,980 --> 00:29:41,600
Henri, je te rejoins.
Henri, I'm coming to you.

643
00:29:42,580 --> 00:29:46,500
Promettez-moi que mon cœur ira rejoindre le sien.
Promise me my heart will find its way to his.

644
00:29:47,360 --> 00:29:48,950
À la flèche.
To the spire.

645
00:29:49,230 --> 00:29:50,430
Je vous le promets.
I promise you.

646
00:29:56,200 --> 00:29:57,240
Coupez, coupez.
Cut, cut.

647
00:29:57,940 --> 00:29:59,360
Magnifique, Isabelle. Bravo.
Magnificent, Isabelle. Bravo.

648
00:30:11,620 --> 00:30:14,720
Vas-y, des plans serrés sur Isabelle, des plans serrés sur Isabelle.
Go on, tight shots on Isabelle, tight shots on Isabelle.

649
00:30:14,840 --> 00:30:15,900
T'en profites pas.
Don't push it.

650
00:30:17,340 --> 00:30:18,700
Isabelle, Isabelle, Isabelle.
Isabelle, Isabelle, Isabelle.

651
00:30:18,700 --> 00:30:20,800
On va faire une dernière prise en plan plus serré.
We'll do one last take with a tighter shot.

652
00:30:21,420 --> 00:30:21,900
Oh, non.
Oh, no.

653
00:30:22,960 --> 00:30:25,040
Excusez-moi, mais j'en suis quand même à ma septième agonie, là.
Excuse me, but this is my seventh death scene, you know.

654
00:30:25,100 --> 00:30:27,360
Cédric, je te rappelle juste que pendant la scène du duel,
Cédric, I'm just reminding you that during the duel scene,

655
00:30:27,400 --> 00:30:28,740
tu m'avais dit que tu manquais de matière.
you told me you felt you didn't have enough material.

656
00:30:29,120 --> 00:30:30,940
Donc moi, je pense que ça coûte rien, là, maintenant.
So I think it costs nothing, right here, right now.

657
00:30:31,180 --> 00:30:31,480
Attends, attends, attends.
Wait, wait, wait.

658
00:30:32,060 --> 00:30:33,540
Excuse-moi, je t'arrête, là.
Sorry, I have to stop you right there.

659
00:30:33,540 --> 00:30:35,180
Parce que le problème, c'est que moi, ça me coûte.
Because the problem is, it does cost me something.

660
00:30:35,640 --> 00:30:36,680
Je ne suis pas une machine, tu vois.
I'm not a machine, you know.

661
00:30:36,740 --> 00:30:38,480
Je meurs pas comme ça sur commande à claquant des doigts.
I don't die on cue just like that, at the snap of a finger.

662
00:30:38,960 --> 00:30:42,300
Je sais bien, Isabelle, mais il faut bien que Cédric puisse monter cette scène en toute sérénité.
I know, Isabelle, but Cédric needs to be able to stage this scene in complete peace of mind.

663
00:30:42,440 --> 00:30:43,580
Ah, mais tout à fait, tout à fait.
Oh, absolutely, absolutely.

664
00:30:43,920 --> 00:30:46,540
Mais toi, il faudrait que t'apprennes à respecter la vision d'un metteur en scène.
But you need to learn to respect a director's vision.

665
00:30:46,540 --> 00:30:49,160
Parce que c'est d'abord ça, la fonction d'une assistante.
Because that's what an assistant is for, first and foremost.

666
00:30:49,500 --> 00:30:51,660
Alors, si Cédric a imaginé sa scène en conséquence,
So if Cédric has imagined his scene a certain way,

667
00:30:51,720 --> 00:30:53,260
c'est peut-être qu'il n'a pas envie d'en faire un clip.
maybe it's because he doesn't want to turn it into a music video.

668
00:30:54,320 --> 00:30:55,200
Tu saisis à la nuance.
You catch the nuance.

669
00:30:55,560 --> 00:30:57,320
Non, mais Isabelle a raison. Il a tout ce qu'il faut.
No, but Isabelle is right. He has everything he needs.

670
00:30:57,700 --> 00:30:58,560
Alors, repose-toi bien.
So get some rest.

671
00:30:58,660 --> 00:31:00,100
Ah, putain, Cédric. Salut.
Oh damn, Cédric. Hey.

672
00:31:40,680 --> 00:31:42,940
En tout cas, c'est drôlement beau, cette solidarité entre agents.
In any case, it's really quite lovely, this solidarity between agents.

673
00:31:44,540 --> 00:31:46,420
Vous n'avez rien de mieux à faire, ce soir ?
Don't you have anything better to do tonight?

674
00:31:46,420 --> 00:31:48,250
Ça me fait plaisir.
My pleasure.

675
00:31:50,320 --> 00:31:51,900
De jouer les chauffeurs privés ?
Playing private chauffeur?

676
00:31:53,110 --> 00:31:54,810
Vous avez de l'eau et des bonbons, là, derrière.
There's water and sweets back there for you.

677
00:31:59,390 --> 00:32:06,810
Allô ? Oui, oui, bien sûr.
Hello? Yes, yes, of course.

678
00:32:06,930 --> 00:32:07,670
Non, non, je suis en route.
No, no, I'm on my way.

679
00:32:07,770 --> 00:32:09,750
Bien sûr, je suis là dans cinq minutes.
Of course, I'll be there in five minutes.

680
00:32:09,910 --> 00:32:10,550
À tout de suite.
See you in a moment.

681
00:32:11,540 --> 00:32:12,780
C'est les Américains ?
Is it the Americans?

682
00:32:14,560 --> 00:32:16,240
Non, c'était Laura Adler.
No, that was Laura Adler.

683
00:32:19,170 --> 00:32:21,670
Elle m'attend pour faire son émission en direct à la radio.
She's waiting for me to do her live radio show.

684
00:32:24,350 --> 00:32:25,850
C'est prévu depuis des semaines.
It's been scheduled for weeks.

685
00:32:25,890 --> 00:32:27,650
Ça m'est complètement sorti de la tête.
It completely slipped my mind.

686
00:32:28,170 --> 00:32:29,590
Ah non, mais c'est pas possible, ça, Isabelle.
Oh no, that's just not on, Isabelle.

687
00:32:29,830 --> 00:32:31,070
Mais Mathias !
But Mathias!

688
00:32:31,070 --> 00:32:32,510
Ça prendra vingt minutes, tout au plus.
It'll take twenty minutes, tops.

689
00:32:33,470 --> 00:32:34,850
Mais je peux pas planter Laura Adler.
But I can't stand up Laura Adler.

690
00:32:35,130 --> 00:32:35,890
Ça se fait pas.
It's just not done.

691
00:32:36,230 --> 00:32:37,920
La question du temps.
The question of time.

692
00:32:38,060 --> 00:32:40,690
Le cœur de mon métier.
The heart of my craft.

693
00:32:45,610 --> 00:32:46,470
Le temps du récit.
Narrative time.

694
00:33:15,490 --> 00:33:16,150
Je passe devant.
I'll go first.

695
00:33:16,570 --> 00:33:18,250
Le but, c'est censure.
The goal is censorship.

696
00:33:19,200 --> 00:33:20,400
Ça allait ? J'étais bien ?
Was it alright? Was I good?

697
00:33:20,400 --> 00:33:20,980
Sans doute.
Most likely.

698
00:33:21,000 --> 00:33:21,020
C'est formidable.
It's wonderful.

699
00:34:22,140 --> 00:34:23,160
Il est où, Gary ?
Where's Gary?

700
00:34:23,720 --> 00:34:24,780
Il nous faut mon chapeau.
We need my hat.

701
00:34:25,140 --> 00:34:27,180
Alex, vous pouvez m'apporter mon chapeau, s'il vous plaît ?
Alex, could you bring me my hat, please?

702
00:34:27,180 --> 00:34:27,540
OK, ben oui.
OK, yeah, sure.

703
00:34:27,720 --> 00:34:28,000
Merci.
Thank you.

704
00:34:28,140 --> 00:34:29,100
Bonsoir, Isabelle.
Good evening, Isabelle.

705
00:34:29,140 --> 00:34:29,620
Bonsoir, Sharon.
Good evening, Sharon.

706
00:34:29,800 --> 00:34:31,160
On n'est pas encore tout à fait prêts.
We're not quite ready yet.

707
00:34:31,600 --> 00:34:34,140
Mais tenez, ça, c'est la scène d'aujourd'hui.
But here, this is today's scene.

708
00:34:35,100 --> 00:34:36,080
Ah ben, je connais mon texte.
Oh, I know my lines.

709
00:34:36,320 --> 00:34:36,760
Of course.
Of course.

710
00:34:42,330 --> 00:34:44,610
Non, mais, Sharon, attendez, attendez.
No, but Sharon, wait, wait.

711
00:34:47,140 --> 00:34:48,600
Non, mais, c'est pas du tout pareil, là.
No, but this is completely different.

712
00:34:48,720 --> 00:34:49,740
C'est beaucoup plus court.
It's much shorter.

713
00:34:49,940 --> 00:34:50,600
Un peu, oui.
A little, yes.

714
00:34:50,780 --> 00:34:52,320
Mais Gary pense que c'est mieux comme ça.
But Gary thinks it works better this way.

715
00:34:52,440 --> 00:34:53,100
C'est plus dynamique.
It's more dynamic.

716
00:34:53,260 --> 00:34:54,780
Ah ben, il est gentil, mais il m'a coupé toutes mes répliques.
Oh, he's sweet, but he's cut all my lines.

717
00:34:54,780 --> 00:34:57,060
Si je peux me permettre, c'est important, le dynamisme, Isabelle.
If I may, dynamism matters, Isabelle.

718
00:34:57,260 --> 00:34:59,240
C'est bien si la scène est rythmée, si elle va vite.
It's good if the scene has rhythm, if it moves fast.

719
00:34:59,600 --> 00:35:00,200
Surtout aujourd'hui.
Especially today.

720
00:35:00,260 --> 00:35:01,220
Oui, Mathias, s'il vous plaît.
Yes, Mathias, please.

721
00:35:01,280 --> 00:35:02,680
Je ne suis pas venue ici pour faire de l'affiguration.
I didn't come here to do background work.

722
00:35:03,000 --> 00:35:03,920
Oui, je comprends.
Yes, I understand.

723
00:35:04,180 --> 00:35:06,200
Je peux jeter un oeil sur votre texte ?
Can I take a look at your script?

724
00:35:06,780 --> 00:35:14,080
Elle est très bien, cette scène.
It's a very good scene, this one.

725
00:35:15,070 --> 00:35:16,370
Il vous en reste pas mal, des répliques.
You've still got quite a few lines left.

726
00:35:16,730 --> 00:35:18,830
Mathias, s'il vous plaît, parlez pas de ce que vous connaissez pas.
Mathias, please don't speak about things you don't know.

727
00:35:18,890 --> 00:35:21,430
Il y avait tout un monologue dont il reste quasiment plus rien.
There was a whole monologue that's been almost entirely cut.

728
00:35:22,170 --> 00:35:23,970
J'ai pas joué une séquence complètement vide de sa substance.
I didn't play a scene completely stripped of its substance.

729
00:35:25,090 --> 00:35:26,830
On a fait des lectures, on a validé des choses.
We did readings, we signed off on things.

730
00:35:27,810 --> 00:35:28,930
Bon, il est où, Gary ?
Right, so where's Gary?

731
00:35:28,930 --> 00:35:30,130
On peut le voir ?
Can we see him?

732
00:35:30,130 --> 00:35:31,470
Il faut qu'on parle de ça ?
Do we need to talk about this?

733
00:35:31,950 --> 00:35:34,390
Pouvez-vous envoyer Gary ici ? Isabelle voudrait le voir, s'il vous plaît.
Could you send Gary in here? Isabelle would like to see him, please.

734
00:35:34,730 --> 00:35:35,650
Oui, maintenant.
Yes, now.

735
00:35:35,930 --> 00:35:36,650
Maintenant, s'il vous plaît.
Now, please.

736
00:35:38,430 --> 00:35:40,390
Ok, allez, merci à tous.
Ok, come on, thank you all.

737
00:35:40,450 --> 00:35:40,810
À jeudi.
See you Thursday.

738
00:35:41,090 --> 00:35:41,990
Revoyez votre texte.
Go over your lines.

739
00:35:53,220 --> 00:35:56,100
Mademoiselle, franchement, dans la scène avec Créon, vous m'avez carrément cueillie.
Miss, honestly, in the scene with Creon, you completely floored me.

740
00:35:56,740 --> 00:35:58,540
Ah ben, merci, c'est gentil.
Oh well, thank you, that's very kind.

741
00:35:58,880 --> 00:36:00,260
Vous avez un agent ?
Do you have an agent?

742
00:36:00,260 --> 00:36:01,120
Euh, non.
Uh, no.

743
00:36:01,380 --> 00:36:02,280
Enfin, pas encore.
Well, not yet.

744
00:36:02,620 --> 00:36:04,320
Alors on va être amenés à se revoir, je crois.
Then I think we'll be seeing each other again.

745
00:36:04,400 --> 00:36:04,700
Tenez.
Here.

746
00:36:05,700 --> 00:36:05,900
Ma carte.
My card.

747
00:36:08,180 --> 00:36:09,660
Ah, vous travaillez chez Reska.
Oh, you work at Reska.

748
00:36:10,440 --> 00:36:11,040
Oh !
Oh!

749
00:36:11,920 --> 00:36:13,820
Vous m'avez juste déboîté l'épaule, mais ça va, merci.
You just dislocated my shoulder, but I'm fine, thanks.

750
00:36:14,080 --> 00:36:15,260
Mais non, je t'ai à peine touché.
Oh come on, I barely touched you.

751
00:36:16,230 --> 00:36:18,070
Ou alors c'est que je contrôle pas trop ma force.
Or maybe I just don't know my own strength.

752
00:36:18,350 --> 00:36:23,690
Euh, juste pour information, t'es en train de parler à Camille Valentini, le nouvel agent chez Reska.
Uh, just so you know, you're talking to Camille Valentini, the new agent at Reska.

753
00:36:23,770 --> 00:36:24,930
Oh, la poule !
Oh wow!

754
00:36:26,020 --> 00:36:26,660
Euh, je...
Uh, I...

755
00:36:26,660 --> 00:36:28,800
Qu'est-ce que je peux faire pour me faire pardonner ?
What can I do to make it up to you?

756
00:36:28,800 --> 00:36:30,600
Bah, aller me chercher un verre de vin, par exemple.
Well, go get me a glass of wine, for starters.

757
00:36:31,240 --> 00:36:34,640
Bon, moi, je suis désolée, je dois vous laisser, mais je vous rappelle et merci beaucoup.
Right, I'm sorry, I have to go, but I'll call you — and thank you so much.

758
00:36:35,020 --> 00:36:36,400
Croyez en votre feu intérieur.
Believe in your inner fire.

759
00:36:37,000 --> 00:36:40,320
Je suis en première année. On a présenté nos travails la semaine dernière.
I'm in first year. We presented our work last week.

760
00:36:40,780 --> 00:36:42,080
Ah bah, c'est bête, j'ai raté ça.
Oh, that's a shame, I missed that.

761
00:36:42,560 --> 00:36:44,780
Ouais. De toute manière, j'avais qu'un petit rôle.
Yeah. Anyway, I only had a small part.

762
00:36:44,980 --> 00:36:47,140
Y a pas de petit rôle, y a que des petits acteurs.
There are no small parts, only small actors.

763
00:36:48,170 --> 00:36:49,150
Merci, c'est cool.
Thanks, that's nice.

764
00:36:49,750 --> 00:36:51,490
Non, mais pardon, c'est une phrase de Stanislavski.
No, but sorry, that's a Stanislavski quote.

765
00:36:52,070 --> 00:36:54,390
Ça veut dire qu'un bon acteur peut briller même dans un petit rôle.
It means a good actor can shine even in a small role.

766
00:36:54,610 --> 00:36:57,030
Bref, j'aurais adoré te voir, même dans un petit rôle. Voilà.
Anyway, I would've loved to see you, even in a small part. That's all.

767
00:36:58,100 --> 00:36:59,000
Et toi, alors ?
And what about you?

768
00:36:59,000 --> 00:36:59,700
Hein ?
Hm?

769
00:36:59,700 --> 00:37:01,920
T'es un petit agent dans une grosse agence, c'est ça ?
You're a junior agent at a big agency, is that it?

770
00:37:02,980 --> 00:37:05,800
C'est ça. Un petit agent plein d'avenir.
That's right. A junior agent with a bright future.

771
00:37:06,680 --> 00:37:08,140
Qui repère les futures grosses stars.
Scouting the next big stars.

772
00:37:08,600 --> 00:37:11,040
Y en a peut-être par ici, on sait jamais.
There might be some around here, you never know.

773
00:37:12,890 --> 00:37:13,950
T'es un agent, toi ?
You're an agent?

774
00:37:14,430 --> 00:37:14,910
Non.
No.

775
00:37:20,180 --> 00:37:22,360
Ok, je dois y aller.
Ok, I have to go.

776
00:37:23,320 --> 00:37:25,330
Bon bah, salut Camille.
Well, bye then, Camille.

777
00:37:25,750 --> 00:37:26,190
Salut.
Bye.

778
00:37:28,240 --> 00:37:29,660
Attends, tu t'appelles comment ?
Wait, what's your name?

779
00:37:30,200 --> 00:37:32,220
Valentin. Comme Valentini, mais sans le i.
Valentin. Like Valentini, but without the i.

780
00:37:33,200 --> 00:37:33,640
Salut.
Bye.

781
00:37:38,680 --> 00:37:43,960
But darling, this is the way we do French women.
But darling, this is the way we do French women.

782
00:37:44,220 --> 00:37:46,560
Enfin, we do French women.
Well, we do French women.

783
00:37:46,840 --> 00:37:48,320
This is the way we do French women.
This is the way we do French women.

784
00:37:48,600 --> 00:37:49,680
C'est bizarre.
That's strange.

785
00:37:50,080 --> 00:37:50,860
Ah oui !
Oh yes!

786
00:37:50,860 --> 00:37:54,500
Et à la fin, il y avait aussi cette référence à l'Américain à Paris que j'aimais beaucoup.
And at the end, there was also that reference to the American in Paris that I really loved.

787
00:37:55,440 --> 00:37:56,900
Donc, on rajoute aussi la fin.
So we'll add the ending back in too.

788
00:37:57,040 --> 00:37:58,080
Yes, it was charming.
Yes, it was charming.

789
00:37:58,460 --> 00:38:02,060
Et d'ailleurs, on pourrait même en profiter pour un tout petit peu la développer,
And actually, we could even take the opportunity to develop it just a little bit,

790
00:38:02,120 --> 00:38:04,660
parce que là, à ce moment-là, je me disais qu'on restait un peu sur sa fin.
because at that point, I felt like it left us a bit hanging.

791
00:38:07,180 --> 00:38:10,260
Mathias, si vous pouviez éviter de faire les 100 pas, parce que là, on essaie de se concentrer,
Mathias, if you could stop pacing, because we're trying to concentrate here,

792
00:38:10,260 --> 00:38:13,000
c'est vraiment très, très pénible. Voilà, merci beaucoup.
it's really very, very distracting. Right, thank you very much.

793
00:38:16,000 --> 00:38:18,920
Alors, voilà. Là, je me souviens, c'était un peu plus long, non ?
Right, okay. I remember it was a bit longer, wasn't it?

794
00:38:21,380 --> 00:38:22,200
Isabelle, you know what ?
Isabelle, you know what?

795
00:38:24,140 --> 00:38:27,900
Here, you write it. Whatever you want to say, go ahead. It's fine with me.
Here, you write it. Whatever you want to say, go ahead. It's fine with me.

796
00:38:28,060 --> 00:38:30,060
Ah non, non, mais on y est, là. C'est très bien comme ça, là.
No, no, we've got it now. It's fine just like this.

797
00:38:31,660 --> 00:38:32,940
Juste la mise en page et puis let's go.
Just the layout and then let's go.

798
00:38:34,870 --> 00:38:37,810
Obstacle surmonté. Je répète, obstacle surmonté.
Obstacle overcome. I repeat, obstacle overcome.

799
00:38:37,830 --> 00:38:39,350
On est toujours dans les temps, ça va marcher.
We're still on schedule, it's going to work.

800
00:38:39,450 --> 00:38:40,310
C'est vrai ?
Really?

801
00:38:40,310 --> 00:38:40,830
Oui, oui, c'est bon.
Yes, yes, we're good.

802
00:38:41,030 --> 00:38:44,170
Oh putain, merci Mathias, je t'aime. Merci. Merci.
Oh God, thank you Mathias, I love you. Thank you. Thank you.

803
00:38:56,140 --> 00:38:57,100
Tout va bien ?
Everything okay?

804
00:38:59,560 --> 00:38:59,860
Oui.
Yes.

805
00:39:00,340 --> 00:39:01,380
Oui, oui.
Yes, yes.

806
00:39:03,490 --> 00:39:05,050
Vous avez besoin de quelque chose ?
Do you need anything?

807
00:39:07,220 --> 00:39:09,940
Non. Non, merci.
No. No, thank you.

808
00:39:10,400 --> 00:39:19,630
Bon, le démarrage était un peu chaotique, c'est vrai, mais là, je vais mettre le turbo.
Okay, the start was a bit chaotic, it's true, but now I'm kicking it into high gear.

809
00:39:19,790 --> 00:39:22,990
Là, il faut être très concentré, aller tout droit et très vite.
We need to stay very focused, go straight ahead and very fast.

810
00:39:23,150 --> 00:39:25,570
Le moindre écart et sortie de route.
One wrong move and we're off the road.

811
00:39:27,280 --> 00:39:28,860
Isabelle, vous avez vu Ben ?
Isabelle, have you seen Ben?

812
00:39:28,860 --> 00:39:29,160
Non.
No.

813
00:39:29,920 --> 00:39:31,240
Sharon ? Sharon !
Sharon? Sharon!

814
00:39:31,240 --> 00:39:31,480
Yeah ?
Yeah?

815
00:39:31,480 --> 00:39:33,100
You seen Ben ?
You seen Ben?

816
00:39:33,700 --> 00:39:34,740
Where is he ?
Where is he?

817
00:39:35,330 --> 00:39:36,330
Ben, c'est Ben Stiller.
Ben, that's Ben Stiller.

818
00:39:36,570 --> 00:39:37,210
Oui, je sais.
Yes, I know.

819
00:39:37,310 --> 00:39:38,770
Très sympa. On s'adore.
Very nice. We adore each other.

820
00:39:39,760 --> 00:39:42,300
Look, he's not coming out of his trailer. He hates the last version.
Look, he's not coming out of his trailer. He hates the last version.

821
00:39:42,380 --> 00:39:42,600
Fucking kidding.
Fucking kidding.

822
00:39:42,640 --> 00:39:43,080
I'm sorry.
I'm sorry.

823
00:39:44,710 --> 00:39:46,070
Sharon, qu'est-ce qui se passe ?
Sharon, what's going on?

824
00:39:47,080 --> 00:39:48,900
Ben n'aime pas la dernière version.
Ben doesn't like the latest version.

825
00:39:49,240 --> 00:39:52,660
Mais comment ça, il n'aime pas ? C'est pas une question d'aimer ou pas ? C'est pour ça que la scène doit se dérouler.
What do you mean he doesn't like it? It's not a matter of liking it or not. That's why the scene has to play out.

826
00:39:53,260 --> 00:39:55,960
Il dit que vous avez coupé tout son texte.
He says you cut all his lines.

827
00:39:58,950 --> 00:40:02,950
Mais regardez pas comme ça, Mathias. Vous avez bien vu ? Moi, je suis dans les starting blocks.
Don't look at me like that, Mathias. You've seen for yourself? I'm already in the starting blocks.

828
00:40:03,570 --> 00:40:07,640
Qu'est-ce qu'il nous fait, Ben Stiller, là ?
What is Ben Stiller doing to us right now?

829
00:40:08,430 --> 00:40:11,450
Il est sympa, mais il peut être aussi très ouf. Control freak.
He's nice, but he can also be pretty intense. Total control freak.

830
00:40:15,370 --> 00:40:17,690
Oui, Gabriel. Vous en êtes tout de ton côté.
Yes, Gabriel. You're just as bad on your end.

831
00:40:18,170 --> 00:40:18,650
Alors, attends.
Okay, hold on.

832
00:40:20,760 --> 00:40:24,220
Bon, ils sont en train de faire la mise en place dans le jardin avec la confidente. Vous êtes déjà sur la route, vous ?
Right, they're setting up in the garden with the confidante. Are you already on your way?

833
00:40:26,540 --> 00:40:29,500
Maintenant, c'est Ben Stiller qui réécrit son texte. On va jamais être arrivé à temps.
Now Ben Stiller is rewriting his lines. We're never going to make it on time.

834
00:40:29,620 --> 00:40:31,790
Oh, putain, non. Oh, non.
Oh, damn it, no. Oh, no.

835
00:40:33,260 --> 00:40:34,900
Si près du but, c'est dur.
So close to the finish line, it's rough.

836
00:40:35,300 --> 00:40:36,960
Non, mais qu'est-ce que je vais leur dire, Mathias ?
But what am I going to tell them, Mathias?

837
00:40:37,980 --> 00:40:39,520
Franchement, je crois qu'on n'a pas le choix.
Honestly, I think we have no choice.

838
00:40:40,310 --> 00:40:42,010
Alors, je dégaine le « je sais ».
Alright, I'm pulling out the "I know."

839
00:40:45,000 --> 00:40:45,600
Allez, courage.
Go on, you've got this.

840
00:41:09,480 --> 00:41:09,920
Isabelle !
Isabelle!

841
00:41:11,190 --> 00:41:11,710
Joanna !
Joanna!

842
00:41:12,030 --> 00:41:16,500
Je sais pas ce qu'elle a. Elle a peut-être fait un malaise.
I don't know what's wrong with her. She might have fainted.

843
00:41:23,040 --> 00:41:30,460
Isabelle, c'est Cédric. Isabelle ! Elle n'est pas là ?
Isabelle, it's Cédric. Isabelle! She's not there?

844
00:41:32,090 --> 00:41:32,590
Je sais.
I know.

845
00:41:33,520 --> 00:41:34,600
On attend pour retourner, là.
We're waiting to go back in.

846
00:41:34,700 --> 00:41:35,200
Je sais.
I know.

847
00:41:35,680 --> 00:41:37,980
Il faut être absolument content de ce soir, là. C'est sa dernière scène.
We absolutely need her in good spirits tonight. It's her last scene.

848
00:41:39,480 --> 00:41:39,960
Je sais.
I know.

849
00:41:40,160 --> 00:41:42,360
Bon, alors, on fait quoi, là ? Gabriel Sarda, là, on fait quoi ?
So what do we do now? Gabriel Sarda, what do we do?

850
00:41:43,580 --> 00:41:44,120
Je sais pas.
I don't know.

851
00:41:44,320 --> 00:41:47,340
Je sais, je sais, je sais, je sais pas, là. Tu sais dire autre chose, là ?
I know, I know, I know, I don't know. Can you say anything else?

852
00:41:48,300 --> 00:41:49,880
Bon, alors, on attend quoi, là ?
So what are we waiting for?

853
00:41:51,710 --> 00:41:55,150
Gabriel, si tu viens voir sur le tournage, c'est peut-être pas pour passer toute la soirée dans ma loge ?
Gabriel, if you're coming to watch the shoot, maybe it's not to spend the whole evening in my dressing room?

854
00:41:55,150 --> 00:41:56,110
T'étais où, là ?
Where were you?

855
00:41:56,110 --> 00:41:59,290
J'étais sur le décor.
I was on set.

856
00:41:59,510 --> 00:42:01,390
Ah, non. On t'a cherché partout pendant une demi-heure, là.
No. We looked everywhere for you for half an hour.

857
00:42:01,830 --> 00:42:03,890
Ah, mais c'est peut-être parce que j'étais partie à la pharmacie de garde.
Oh, well, maybe because I'd gone to the late-night pharmacy.

858
00:42:05,260 --> 00:42:07,020
Je voulais rester discrète. J'ai des ballonnements.
I wanted to be discreet. I have bloating.

859
00:42:08,410 --> 00:42:10,030
J'avais peut-être pas envie que tout le monde le sache.
Maybe I didn't want everyone to know about it.

860
00:42:10,730 --> 00:42:13,610
OK. Et quand tu veux aller discrètement à la pharmacie, tu y vas comme ça ?
OK. And when you want to sneak off to the pharmacy, you go like that?

861
00:42:15,130 --> 00:42:16,450
Ben, oui. Je vois pas où est le problème.
Well, yes. I don't see the problem.

862
00:42:17,090 --> 00:42:20,980
Ouh, si t'es dehors, t'es très conventionnel, hein, Cédric.
Oh, you're very conventional when you're outside, aren't you, Cédric.

863
00:42:22,380 --> 00:42:23,720
Bon, ben, on t'attend sur le décor.
Right, well, we'll see you on set.

864
00:42:23,840 --> 00:42:26,310
D'accord. À tout de suite.
OK. See you in a minute.

865
00:42:26,410 --> 00:42:29,920
Et comment t'as fait ?
And how did you manage it?

866
00:42:29,920 --> 00:42:32,720
Ben, ça a complètement dégénéré entre le metteur en scène et Ben Stiller.
Well, things completely fell apart between the director and Ben Stiller.

867
00:42:32,800 --> 00:42:34,900
Elle se sent presque venue aux mains. Le chef a observé et mêlé.
It nearly came to blows. The chief stepped in and got involved.

868
00:42:35,020 --> 00:42:36,420
Du coup, je lui ai dit que ça lui méritait pas terrible.
So I told him it really wasn't worth it.

869
00:42:37,300 --> 00:42:41,060
On s'est commencé à tirer dans tous les sens. Résultat, tournage interrompu.
We started pulling in every direction. Result — shoot suspended.

870
00:42:41,620 --> 00:42:42,520
C'est cool, non ?
Pretty cool, right?

871
00:42:43,300 --> 00:42:44,440
Mais comment t'es changé ?
But how did you change so fast?

872
00:42:45,160 --> 00:42:47,440
T'as vu un peu ? Je peux aussi jouer Arturo Brachetti.
Not bad, right? I could play Arturo Brachetti too.

873
00:42:48,260 --> 00:42:48,880
Ça y va ?
You OK?

874
00:43:08,170 --> 00:43:08,730
Merci, Mathias.
Thank you, Mathias.

875
00:43:10,000 --> 00:43:12,680
Je crois que sans toi, je serais en train de me faire virer par Richard.
I think without you, I'd be getting fired by Richard right now.

876
00:43:14,430 --> 00:43:15,750
C'est pour ça que tu veux partir ?
Is that why you want to leave?

877
00:43:17,420 --> 00:43:19,460
Pour pas qu'un jour, c'est celui qui te vire ?
So that one day it's not him firing you?

878
00:43:19,580 --> 00:43:20,640
Je suis au courant, Gabriel.
I'm aware, Gabriel.

879
00:43:21,500 --> 00:43:23,860
Les gens immobiliers qui s'occupent de vos bureaux, je le connais.
The real estate people handling your offices — I know him.

880
00:43:26,060 --> 00:43:28,080
Moi aussi, j'ai eu envie de partir, plus d'une fois.
I've wanted to leave too, more than once.

881
00:43:28,480 --> 00:43:29,260
Mais j'aime trop Esca.
But I love Esca too much.

882
00:43:30,780 --> 00:43:31,860
Faut qu'on reste solidaires.
We have to stick together.

883
00:43:32,420 --> 00:43:33,540
Un peu comme cette nuit, tu vois.
A bit like tonight, you know.

884
00:43:35,400 --> 00:43:37,540
Je sais bien qu'entre toi et moi, souvent, c'est tendu.
I know things between you and me are often tense.

885
00:43:37,560 --> 00:43:39,700
Je sais bien qu'Andréa ne me porte pas la main.
I know Andréa doesn't exactly hold me in high regard.

886
00:43:39,720 --> 00:43:40,940
Pas particulièrement dans son cœur.
Not particularly close to her heart.

887
00:43:41,320 --> 00:43:42,240
On est une famille.
We're a family.

888
00:43:43,220 --> 00:43:44,780
Et l'intrus dans cette famille, c'est Richard.
And the outsider in this family is Richard.

889
00:43:48,790 --> 00:43:51,270
S'il partait, vous resteriez ?
If he left, would you stay?

890
00:44:00,720 --> 00:44:01,880
Encore merci, les garçons.
Thank you again, boys.

891
00:44:02,020 --> 00:44:02,320
De rien.
Don't mention it.

892
00:44:02,900 --> 00:44:03,740
Et repose-toi.
And get some rest.

893
00:44:03,920 --> 00:44:04,280
Oui.
Yes.

894
00:44:06,020 --> 00:44:07,820
Je vais d'abord faire un petit saut au défilé Chanel.
I'll just pop by the Chanel show first.

895
00:44:08,770 --> 00:44:10,150
C'est la fachomique, en ce moment.
It's the hot thing right now.

896
00:44:12,000 --> 00:44:13,040
Je vous embrasse.
Kisses.

897
00:44:21,820 --> 00:44:23,880
Si je comprends bien, cette femme ne dort jamais.
If I understand correctly, this woman never sleeps.

898
00:44:24,660 --> 00:44:33,720
Je finis ta compote, Andréa.
I'm finishing your compote, Andréa.

899
