1085
00:53:43,420 --> 00:53:44,660
Donc, je viens de Clermont-Ferrand.
So, I'm from Clermont-Ferrand.

1086
00:53:44,800 --> 00:53:44,940
Ouais.
Yeah.

1087
00:53:47,280 --> 00:53:49,260
J'avoue que les études, c'était pas trop mon truc.
I'll be honest, school was never really my thing.

1088
00:53:49,440 --> 00:53:50,640
Donc, j'ai pas mon bac.
So I don't have my baccalauréat.

1089
00:53:51,400 --> 00:53:52,360
Le bac, le bac.
The bac, the bac.

1090
00:53:53,140 --> 00:53:53,980
C'est clair.
Fair enough.

1091
00:53:54,940 --> 00:53:57,660
Et puis après, je suis monté à Paris il y a deux ans.
And then I moved to Paris two years ago.

1092
00:53:57,880 --> 00:53:58,500
Par amour.
For love.

1093
00:53:59,160 --> 00:53:59,840
Ah, c'est bien.
Oh, that's nice.

1094
00:54:00,180 --> 00:54:03,460
Et puis, mon ami est reparti et moi, je suis resté.
And then my partner left and I stayed.

1095
00:54:04,180 --> 00:54:04,800
Ah, c'est mieux.
Oh, even better.

1096
00:54:07,930 --> 00:54:08,830
Et toi, alors ?
What about you?

1097
00:54:09,350 --> 00:54:10,950
Comment t'es devenu agent d'acteur ?
How did you become a talent agent?

1098
00:54:10,950 --> 00:54:13,070
Y a des études pour ça ou...
Is there a degree for that, or...

1099
00:54:13,070 --> 00:54:15,470
Oui, alors le mieux, c'est de commencer par des études de vétérinaire.
Yes, well, the best way is to start with a veterinary degree.

1100
00:54:17,940 --> 00:54:20,020
Non, sérieusement, j'ai toujours adoré le cinéma, moi.
No, seriously, I've always loved cinema.

1101
00:54:21,840 --> 00:54:24,020
Ma mère m'a emmenée voir des tonnes de films d'art et d'essai
My mother took me to see tons of arthouse films

1102
00:54:24,020 --> 00:54:24,660
quand j'étais enfant.
when I was a child.

1103
00:54:25,260 --> 00:54:27,040
Et en fait, j'ai commencé par être assistant.
And actually, I started out as an assistant.

1104
00:54:28,090 --> 00:54:28,410
C'est ça.
Right.

1105
00:54:28,430 --> 00:54:32,130
Et puis, j'ai été promu agent cette année
And then I was promoted to agent this year

1106
00:54:32,130 --> 00:54:34,390
pour développer mon propre fichier et voilà.
to build my own roster, and here we are.

1107
00:54:35,600 --> 00:54:37,840
J'ai ramené quelques photos et...
I brought some photos and...

1108
00:54:38,420 --> 00:54:39,440
Une bande des mots.
A showreel.

1109
00:54:40,000 --> 00:54:40,820
Ah ouais ?
Oh yeah?

1110
00:54:40,820 --> 00:54:40,980
Ouais.
Yeah.

1111
00:54:41,460 --> 00:54:44,380
J'ai fait rapidement cette nuit, spécialement pour toi.
I put it together quickly last night, specially for you.

1112
00:54:45,840 --> 00:54:47,660
Je vais les regarder avec la plus grande attention.
I'll watch them with the greatest attention.

1113
00:54:51,280 --> 00:54:53,300
Je connais pas trop les règles dans le métier,
I don't really know the rules in this business,

1114
00:54:53,320 --> 00:54:55,690
mais si on est amenés à travailler ensemble,
but if we end up working together,

1115
00:54:56,530 --> 00:54:57,790
je pourrais quand même t'embrasser.
could I still kiss you?

1116
00:54:58,940 --> 00:55:01,060
Mais on travaille pas encore ensemble, que je sache.
But we're not working together yet, as far as I know.

1117
00:55:22,560 --> 00:55:23,000
Pardon.
Sorry.

1118
00:55:25,380 --> 00:55:25,620
Bon.
Right.

1119
00:55:27,210 --> 00:55:28,550
Visiblement, Mathias connaît le mec de l'agence.
Apparently Mathias knows the guy from the agency.

1120
00:55:28,750 --> 00:55:30,050
C'est comme ça qu'il a su pour les bureaux, quoi.
That's how he found out about the offices.

1121
00:55:30,450 --> 00:55:31,720
Moi, j'ai essayé de le calmer.
I tried to calm him down.

1122
00:55:31,800 --> 00:55:33,320
J'ai lui expliqué qu'on était qu'à état de réflexion,
I explained that we were just in the thinking stage,

1123
00:55:33,340 --> 00:55:34,340
que c'était pas du tout avancé, quoi.
that nothing was set in stone at all.

1124
00:55:36,640 --> 00:55:38,480
Arrête avec la chantilly, c'est chiant, ce bruit-là.
Stop with the whipped cream, that noise is so annoying.

1125
00:55:38,540 --> 00:55:39,100
Pardon, excuse-moi.
Sorry, excuse me.

1126
00:55:40,240 --> 00:55:42,180
Tu sais, il a été... Il a été gentil.
You know, he was... he was kind.

1127
00:55:42,780 --> 00:55:43,020
Vraiment.
Really.

1128
00:55:43,200 --> 00:55:44,400
Et il m'a vachement aidé cette nuit.
And he helped me a lot last night.

1129
00:55:45,340 --> 00:55:46,780
Méfie-toi de lui, je te l'ai toujours dit.
Watch out for him, I've always told you.

1130
00:55:47,700 --> 00:55:48,940
Capable du meilleur comme du pire.
He's capable of the best and the worst.

1131
00:55:49,560 --> 00:55:50,220
Ah, excuse-moi.
Oh, excuse me.

1132
00:55:51,890 --> 00:55:52,670
Ah bon, c'est Isabelle.
Oh, it's Isabelle.

1133
00:55:53,370 --> 00:55:54,170
Je te laisse, hein.
I'll let you go.

1134
00:55:54,510 --> 00:55:55,030
Je dois te laisser.
I have to go.

1135
00:55:55,030 --> 00:55:56,170
Je t'embrasse fort.
Big kiss.

1136
00:55:56,410 --> 00:55:56,790
Repose-toi.
Get some rest.

1137
00:55:56,870 --> 00:55:57,430
D'accord ?
Okay?

1138
00:55:58,060 --> 00:55:58,340
Salut.
Bye.

1139
00:56:02,080 --> 00:56:03,180
Ça va, Isabelle ?
How are you, Isabelle?

1140
00:56:04,910 --> 00:56:05,610
Excuse-moi, je...
Sorry, I...

1141
00:56:06,010 --> 00:56:06,790
Je t'entends pas du tout.
I can't hear you at all.

1142
00:56:06,870 --> 00:56:07,390
Y a pas de son, là.
There's no sound.

1143
00:56:08,710 --> 00:56:09,390
J'entends pas.
I can't hear you.

1144
00:56:09,450 --> 00:56:09,990
Je te rappelle.
I'll call you back.

1145
00:56:14,750 --> 00:56:15,790
Comment ça, plus de voix ?
What do you mean, no voice?

1146
00:56:17,220 --> 00:56:18,260
Et la cortisone ?
What about the cortisone?

1147
00:56:24,200 --> 00:56:25,160
Plus aucun effet ?
Not working anymore?

1148
00:56:27,800 --> 00:56:28,720
Bon, elle a vu le médecin.
Right, she's seen the doctor.

1149
00:56:29,020 --> 00:56:29,300
Voilà.
There you go.

1150
00:56:29,400 --> 00:56:30,520
Elle est arrêtée pendant une semaine.
She's off for a week.

1151
00:56:30,660 --> 00:56:31,820
Du coup, le tournage américain aussi.
Which means the American shoot too.

1152
00:56:32,500 --> 00:56:34,100
Et qu'est-ce qui se passe dans ces cas-là ?
And what happens in cases like that?

1153
00:56:34,100 --> 00:56:35,880
Oh, ben, c'est un accident du travail, hein.
Oh, well, it's a workplace accident, isn't it.

1154
00:56:36,200 --> 00:56:36,480
Classique.
Classic.

1155
00:56:37,380 --> 00:56:39,680
Les assurances prennent en charge les frais d'interruption du tournage.
Insurance covers the costs of the production shutdown.

1156
00:56:40,020 --> 00:56:42,020
Bah, vous, des acteurs qui tombent malades, ça arrive tout le temps.
Well, actors getting sick happens all the time.

1157
00:56:42,540 --> 00:56:45,180
Ouais, non, mais parce que j'imagine qu'une semaine d'interruption sur un film comme ça,
Yeah, no, but I imagine a week's shutdown on a film like that

1158
00:56:45,220 --> 00:56:46,040
ça coûte un paquet de pognon.
costs a hell of a lot of money.

1159
00:56:46,240 --> 00:56:48,180
Ça devrait faire dans les quelques millions de dollars.
Should be somewhere in the millions of dollars.

1160
00:56:48,640 --> 00:56:48,920
Oui.
Yes.

1161
00:56:49,220 --> 00:56:50,740
C'est ce que j'ai toujours compris des assurances.
That's always been my understanding of insurance.

1162
00:56:50,760 --> 00:56:52,600
En général, quand il faut payer, elles aiment bien chercher la petite bête.
Generally, when it comes time to pay, they love to nitpick.

1163
00:56:52,840 --> 00:56:55,320
Ah, ça, c'est sûr qu'elles vont emmerder les Américains.
Oh, they'll definitely give the Americans a hard time.

1164
00:56:55,860 --> 00:56:58,640
Elles doivent même déjà être en train de pinailler sur les conditions de travail,
They're probably already quibbling over working conditions,

1165
00:56:58,720 --> 00:56:59,420
les heures sup'.
overtime hours.

1166
00:56:59,420 --> 00:57:00,340
J'espère qu'ils sont en règle.
I hope they're compliant.

1167
00:57:00,740 --> 00:57:02,100
Nous, on l'est pas avec nos deux films.
We're not, with our two films.

1168
00:57:03,010 --> 00:57:04,710
Les Américains pourraient très bien se retourner contre nous,
The Americans could very well turn on us,

1169
00:57:04,750 --> 00:57:05,570
nous faire porter le chapeau, là.
pin the blame on us.

1170
00:57:05,590 --> 00:57:07,150
Non, mais arrêtez d'élucubrer, là !
Come on, stop spinning theories!

1171
00:57:07,590 --> 00:57:09,230
Mais non, les assurances feront leur boulot,
No, the insurers will do their job,

1172
00:57:09,330 --> 00:57:11,710
les Américains sauront rien au sujet d'Isabelle, et voilà, tout ira bien.
the Americans won't find out anything about Isabelle, and that'll be that.

1173
00:57:12,640 --> 00:57:13,340
Si tu le dis.
If you say so.

1174
00:57:13,740 --> 00:57:15,900
C'est vrai qu'il est ultra photogénique.
He is incredibly photogenic, that's true.

1175
00:57:16,280 --> 00:57:18,640
Non, il est sublime avec sa faussette, là.
No, he's stunning with that little falsetto.

1176
00:57:19,180 --> 00:57:22,690
Oui, mais ça suffit pas, non ? On est d'accord ?
Sure, but that's not enough, is it? We agree on that?

1177
00:57:24,720 --> 00:57:27,660
Attends, il a rien fait, il a fait de la figure et trois courts-métrages autoproduits.
Come on, he's done nothing — some extra work and three self-produced short films.

1178
00:57:27,820 --> 00:57:29,600
Non, mais c'est toi qui est hyper snob, en fait.
No, you're the one being a total snob here.

1179
00:57:29,780 --> 00:57:32,280
On va prendre que des acteurs du conservatoire national de la dramatique.
What, we're only going to cast graduates from the national drama conservatory?

1180
00:57:32,940 --> 00:57:34,700
Bon, bah, on va vite être fixés.
Well, we'll find out soon enough.

1181
00:57:35,730 --> 00:57:37,530
Tu sais, je fréquence le milieu depuis assez longtemps
You know, I've been around this industry long enough

1182
00:57:37,530 --> 00:57:39,170
pour avoir développé un instinct très sûr,
to have developed a very reliable instinct,

1183
00:57:39,210 --> 00:57:40,230
même sur un acteur inexplicable.
even for an unconventional actor.

1184
00:57:41,400 --> 00:57:43,300
Bon, bah, très bien. On va voir ça.
Alright, fine. We'll see about that.

1185
00:57:53,180 --> 00:57:55,000
À trois ans.
At three years old.

1186
00:57:57,020 --> 00:58:03,920
C'est beau, cette amplitude de gestes.
That sweep of gestures is something.

1187
00:58:38,880 --> 00:58:43,780
Pardon, mais sur une échelle de la déceptitude, il est à combien, ton instinct, là ? Dis-moi.
Sorry, but on a scale of disappointment, where does your instinct land right now? Tell me.

1188
00:58:44,440 --> 00:58:44,920
Non !
No!

1189
00:58:44,940 --> 00:58:45,380
Tu veux dire ça ?
You're seriously going with that?

1190
00:58:45,780 --> 00:58:47,920
Non, mais attends, il a fait ça tout seul, chez lui, la nuit.
No, but hang on — he did that on his own, at home, at night.

1191
00:58:48,380 --> 00:58:51,760
Ça manque de mise en forme, de lumière, mais c'est normal, hein.
It's rough around the edges, no real lighting, but that's to be expected.

1192
00:58:51,760 --> 00:58:52,400
C'est très brut.
It's very raw.

1193
00:58:52,940 --> 00:58:54,080
Non, arrête, c'est une quiche.
No, stop — he's terrible.

1194
00:58:54,480 --> 00:58:55,360
Non, je suis pas d'accord.
I disagree.

1195
00:58:55,660 --> 00:58:57,800
C'est très spécial, c'est novateur, justement.
It's very unique, it's actually innovative.

1196
00:58:58,080 --> 00:58:59,880
C'est drôle que tu vois pas.
It's funny you don't see it.

1197
00:59:00,680 --> 00:59:02,680
Très grands acteurs, aussi, avaient un jeu un peu particulier.
Even great actors had a somewhat unusual style.

1198
00:59:02,740 --> 00:59:04,160
Ça les a pas empêchés de réussir, Camille.
It didn't stop them from succeeding, Camille.

1199
00:59:04,340 --> 00:59:07,200
Jean-Pierre Léo, Mathieu Amalric, Belmondo.
Jean-Pierre Léaud, Mathieu Amalric, Belmondo.

1200
00:59:07,260 --> 00:59:09,940
Attends, Belmondo, au début, personne n'y croyait.
Come on — Belmondo, nobody believed in him at first.

1201
00:59:10,000 --> 00:59:11,700
Il a été requelé deux fois du conservatoire, donc...
He's been rejected from the conservatory twice, so...

1202
00:59:11,700 --> 00:59:14,380
Non, mais attends, lui, sa seule chance, c'est de faire un spectacle comique involontaire.
No, but wait — his only shot is to be some kind of accidental comedy act.

1203
00:59:15,160 --> 00:59:16,600
Camille Valentine représente pas ce mec.
Camille Valentine is not representing this guy.

1204
00:59:16,760 --> 00:59:17,300
Moi, j'y crois.
I believe in him.

1205
00:59:17,520 --> 00:59:19,780
Je trouve qu'on peut pas passer à côté d'un physique pareil, je suis désolée.
I'm sorry, but you can't ignore a look like that.

1206
00:59:20,100 --> 00:59:21,680
T'as senti tout ce qu'il y a à l'intérieur ?
Did you feel everything that's underneath?

1207
00:59:22,360 --> 00:59:24,020
Il a un potentiel énorme.
He has enormous potential.

1208
00:59:24,580 --> 00:59:25,640
En fait, tu parles pour qui, là ?
So who are you actually speaking for right now?

1209
00:59:25,640 --> 00:59:27,740
Tu parles pour nous ou tu parles pour toi ?
Are you speaking for us, or for yourself?

1210
00:59:27,740 --> 00:59:29,940
Je vais le faire travailler, je vais le faire répéter, je serai son pig-maillon.
I'm going to work with him, rehearse with him — I'll be his Pygmalion.

1211
00:59:30,100 --> 00:59:30,960
Je te jure, je peux en faire une star.
I swear, I can make him a star.

1212
00:59:31,160 --> 00:59:32,140
Un jour, tu me remercieras.
One day you'll thank me.

1213
00:59:32,320 --> 00:59:33,320
La France, elle se me remerciera.
France itself will thank me.

1214
00:59:44,850 --> 00:59:45,810
OK, OK, on le prend.
OK, OK, we'll take him.

1215
00:59:54,800 --> 00:59:55,600
Parfois, tu me fais peur.
Sometimes you scare me.

1216
00:59:56,140 --> 00:59:56,740
Oh, bah non.
Oh, come on.

1217
00:59:56,740 --> 01:00:01,020
Elle est magnifique, cette photo.
It's a beautiful photo.

1218
01:00:01,790 --> 01:00:02,550
Merci beaucoup.
Thank you very much.

1219
01:00:02,750 --> 01:00:03,570
C'est vrai que ça manquait.
It was really missing something.

1220
01:00:04,010 --> 01:00:04,650
C'est...
It's...

1221
01:00:05,880 --> 01:00:07,100
Ça va, toi ?
Are you doing OK?

1222
01:00:09,730 --> 01:00:11,620
Je m'en veux.
I blame myself.

1223
01:00:11,960 --> 01:00:12,840
J'en fais trop.
I'm overdoing it.

1224
01:00:14,100 --> 01:00:16,180
Je vais prendre des risques à considérer à tout le monde.
I'm going to take risks that affect everyone.

1225
01:00:16,700 --> 01:00:17,360
Mais non.
No, you're not.

1226
01:00:19,730 --> 01:00:21,890
Et dis-moi, t'es sûre que...
And tell me, are you sure that...

1227
01:00:24,240 --> 01:00:27,740
T'es sûre que l'assurance, elle va pouvoir prendre en charge l'interruption du tournage ?
Are you sure the insurance will cover the production shutdown?

1228
01:00:27,740 --> 01:00:28,520
C'est pas ton problème.
That's not your problem.

1229
01:00:29,000 --> 01:00:29,600
C'est...
It's...

1230
01:00:30,040 --> 01:00:31,900
C'est le problème des producteurs, des banquiers.
That's the producers' and financiers' problem.

1231
01:00:32,060 --> 01:00:32,920
Y a des gens qui font ça.
There are people who handle that.

1232
01:00:33,100 --> 01:00:35,100
Toi, tu te reposes et tu reviens très vite en forme.
You rest up and come back fighting fit real soon.

1233
01:00:35,240 --> 01:00:36,000
C'est sûr.
Absolutely.

1234
01:00:36,120 --> 01:00:37,360
C'est sûr que je ne bouge plus, là, maintenant.
One thing's for sure — I'm not moving from here, not right now.

1235
01:00:37,600 --> 01:00:37,700
Bon.
Right.

1236
01:00:37,880 --> 01:00:40,360
Tu bookings, tu te prélasses, tu fais des...
You just book things, lounge around, do your...

1237
01:00:48,570 --> 01:00:49,150
C'est...
It's...

1238
01:00:49,150 --> 01:00:52,590
C'est un ami que j'héberge pour quelque temps.
He's a friend I'm putting up for a while.

1239
01:00:53,090 --> 01:00:53,730
Mais c'est...
But it's...

1240
01:00:53,730 --> 01:00:56,090
Il s'en est où, le rédacteur coréen ?
Where's the Korean writer at?

1241
01:00:57,760 --> 01:00:58,120
Euh...
Uh...

1242
01:00:59,730 --> 01:01:00,090
Oui.
Yeah.

1243
01:01:01,190 --> 01:01:03,110
Non, mais il est juste de passage à Paris, là.
No, he's just passing through Paris.

1244
01:01:03,490 --> 01:01:04,900
Mais tu fais quoi, là ?
But what are you doing here?

1245
01:01:04,900 --> 01:01:07,050
Mais tu tournes un film ?
Are you shooting a film?

1246
01:01:07,050 --> 01:01:08,130
Mais non, pas vraiment.
Well, not exactly.

1247
01:01:08,290 --> 01:01:08,910
C'est juste un...
It's just a...

1248
01:01:08,910 --> 01:01:10,990
C'est un petit film, comme ça, expérimental.
It's a small experimental film, sort of.

1249
01:01:11,530 --> 01:01:13,090
J'avais quelques jours de libre, alors...
I had a few free days, so...

1250
01:01:13,530 --> 01:01:15,810
Chine m'a demandé de faire ça vite fait bien fait.
China asked me to knock something out quickly.

1251
01:01:17,580 --> 01:01:17,940
Voilà.
That's it.

1252
01:01:19,780 --> 01:01:20,920
C'est le sort d'une femme bête.
That's the fate of a foolish woman.

1253
01:01:21,710 --> 01:01:23,010
Oui, mais c'est pas possible, ça.
Yes, but this can't go on.

1254
01:01:23,090 --> 01:01:23,490
Il faut...
You need to...

1255
01:01:23,930 --> 01:01:25,150
Il faut que tu te reposes.
You need to rest.

1256
01:01:25,290 --> 01:01:26,250
Mais on s'amuse.
But we're having fun.

1257
01:01:27,090 --> 01:01:29,010
Pas de dialogue, pas de contrat, pas de producteur.
No dialogue, no contract, no producer.

1258
01:01:29,610 --> 01:01:30,450
Juste la caméra.
Just the camera.

1259
01:01:31,650 --> 01:01:32,230
Et moi.
And me.

1260
01:01:39,980 --> 01:01:40,760
Ah, c'est...
Ah, that's...

1261
01:01:45,850 --> 01:01:47,250
Préserver l'intégrité d'A.S.K.
Preserving A.S.K.'s integrity.

1262
01:01:48,930 --> 01:01:53,590
De faire rester Gabriel et Andrea tout en faisant partir Hicham.
Keeping Gabriel and Andrea while getting rid of Hicham.

1263
01:01:53,970 --> 01:01:57,510
Ma pote, ça !
That's my girl!

1264
01:01:57,510 --> 01:01:57,690
Oui.
Yes.

1265
01:01:58,100 --> 01:01:58,560
Ah !
Ah!

1266
01:02:01,900 --> 01:02:02,080
Risqué.
Risky.

1267
01:02:02,320 --> 01:02:04,340
Pour qui ? Pour vous ?
For whom? For you?

1268
01:02:04,340 --> 01:02:05,760
Pour moi.
For me.

1269
01:02:05,900 --> 01:02:06,720
Pour l'agence.
For the agency.

1270
01:02:06,720 --> 01:02:07,080
Non.
No.

1271
01:02:11,180 --> 01:02:11,580
Attendez.
Wait.

1272
01:02:11,780 --> 01:02:13,020
J'ai quelque chose.
I have something.

1273
01:02:17,950 --> 01:02:18,750
Le yiqing.
The I Ching.

1274
01:02:18,930 --> 01:02:19,430
C'est quoi ?
What is it?

1275
01:02:19,430 --> 01:02:21,350
C'est extraordinaire.
It's extraordinary.

1276
01:02:21,980 --> 01:02:23,620
C'est une méthode chinoise.
It's a Chinese method.

1277
01:02:25,000 --> 01:02:26,200
C'est un grand texte.
It's a great text.

1278
01:02:26,560 --> 01:02:30,780
En fait, ça aide à savoir où on en est, ce qu'on veut faire, à prendre des décisions.
It helps you understand where you stand, what you want to do, how to make decisions.

1279
01:02:31,140 --> 01:02:32,900
Et moi, dans ma vie, je m'en suis servie, mais...
And in my life, I've used it, but...

1280
01:02:33,380 --> 01:02:34,020
Tellement de fois.
So many times.

1281
01:02:34,400 --> 01:02:36,720
Et la dernière fois, vous savez quand c'était ?
And do you know when the last time was?

1282
01:02:38,710 --> 01:02:41,270
La nuit où votre femme m'a présenté Alexandre.
The night your wife introduced me to Alexandre.

1283
01:02:42,060 --> 01:02:44,180
Le yiqing, il m'a parlé de notre lien.
The I Ching spoke to me about our bond.

1284
01:02:45,200 --> 01:02:46,140
Il m'a dit que...
It told me that...

1285
01:02:46,140 --> 01:02:47,660
Il était en train de se transformer.
It was in the process of transforming.

1286
01:02:47,660 --> 01:02:48,830
De s'équilibrer.
Of finding balance.

1287
01:02:49,300 --> 01:02:50,760
Qu'il allait s'inscrire dans la durée.
That it would stand the test of time.

1288
01:02:51,220 --> 01:02:53,000
Et au petit matin, vous étiez là.
And by morning, there you were.

1289
01:03:32,540 --> 01:03:33,540
Mathias, c'est génial.
Mathias, this is brilliant.

1290
01:03:33,980 --> 01:03:35,080
C'est la percée.
It's the breakthrough.

1291
01:03:42,440 --> 01:03:43,420
Une percée.
A breakthrough.

1292
01:03:43,840 --> 01:03:45,560
Après une longue tension accumulée.
After a long buildup of tension.

1293
01:03:45,820 --> 01:03:48,760
Comme la brèche d'un fleuve fait à travers ses digues.
Like a river breaking through its dikes.

1294
01:03:48,940 --> 01:03:50,380
Comme un nuage qui crève.
Like a cloud bursting.

1295
01:03:50,880 --> 01:04:00,280
Où les hommes vulgaires sont en voie de disparition.
Where lesser men are fading away.

1296
01:04:01,130 --> 01:04:06,330
Une action résolue fait que le changement des conditions amène la percée.
Resolute action brings about a change in conditions that leads to the breakthrough.

1297
01:04:06,790 --> 01:04:08,090
Non, mais c'est fou, Mathias.
No, but this is incredible, Mathias.

1298
01:04:08,090 --> 01:04:09,430
Ça veut dire que c'est maintenant.
It means now is the time.

1299
01:04:10,310 --> 01:04:11,870
Allez-y, Mathias.
Go ahead, Mathias.

1300
01:04:12,930 --> 01:04:13,250
Percez.
Break through.

1301
01:04:14,230 --> 01:04:14,550
Percez.
Break through.

1302
01:05:03,650 --> 01:05:04,950
Bonsoir, je voudrais un coursier, s'il vous plaît.
Good evening, I'd like a courier, please.

1303
01:05:06,440 --> 01:05:07,620
Paris, 1er arrondissement.
Paris, 1st arrondissement.

1304
01:05:07,860 --> 01:05:08,180
...
...
